ItemTooltip: {
	Generic: {
		CheckTheAEM: "[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Gold}:Press NOT YET BOUND to check the All-Encompassing Menu's entry for this item!]"
		EdibleFromNormalUse:
			'''
			Using this item from the hotbar while holding the Swallow Item keybind causes you to swallow it
			If this is a stack of multiple items, this only swallows items one at a time unless otherwise stated
			'''
		EatenByNormalUse:
			'''
			Using this item from the hotbar at all causes you to swallow it
			If this is a stack of multiple items, this only swallows items one at a time unless otherwise stated
			'''
		Broken:
			'''
			This item has been damaged too heavily for continued use and has become non-functional
			Broken items can be repaired with the Scroll of Divine Indigestion or by visiting St. Promethia
			'''
		StruggleDamageBoost: +{StrDmgUp} base struggle damage when held in a gut

		HungryPlaceable: {
			DefaultHungry: Has a lingering appetite (which can be quelled)
			DefaultNormal: Has a dormant appetite (which can be awakened)
		}

		AcidResistTier: {
			0: Does not resist any stomach acids
			1: Immune to normal stomach acids
			2: Immune to normal and enchanted stomach acids
			3: Immune to normal and enchanted stomach acids, as well as aqua regia
			99: Digesting this item requires acids blessed by the gods themselves

			100: {
				Normal: Indigestible...?
				Chronological: Indigestible...but not for you
			}
		}

		Food: {
			Short: The satisfaction of a good meal lingers longer after digesting this item
			Long: This item counts twice as much towards Well Fed's buff while digesting.
		}

		LongTooltipHelpers: {
			ColdTemperatureRules:
				'''
				[c/7F7F7F:You are considered in the cold when one or more of the following is true:]
				[c/7F7F7F:- You are in the Tundra and not standing on tiles classified as hot]
				[c/7F7F7F:- You are standing on Ice or Snow in a biome not classified as hot]
				'''
			SunlightExposureRules:
				'''
				[c/7F7F7F:You are considered exposed to sunlight when all of the following are true:]
				[c/7F7F7F:- You are above 0']
				[c/7F7F7F:- You are not in front of a background wall]
				[c/7F7F7F:- It is daytime]
				'''
		}
	}

	Vanilla: {
		Accessories: {
			Informational: {
				REK3K: Displays number of enemies, kill and meal counts, and rare creatures
				TallyCounter:
					'''
					Displays how many enemies have been killed in the world
					Displays how many entities you've digested
					'''
			}

			Offensive: {
				SharkToothNecklace:
					'''
					Grants a light amount of armor penetration
					Slightly improves your throat and acids
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
			}

			Pets: {
				Light: {
					CandyFairyMasterPetItem: {
						Short:
							'''
							Summons a self-proclaimed fairy princess to provide light and guard you from certain mobs (by eating them)
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							Summons a small prismatic fairy who calls herself the Heiress of Light. Her real name is Radianne.
							The Heiress [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:provides light in dark places].
							The Heiress [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:will hunt down and eat nearby mobs] which are shiny or twinkly enough for her tastes (including other fairies), as well as royalty.
							Her stats are as follows:
							[c/7F7F7F:> Health:] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:{MiniCandyFairyMaxHealth}]
							[c/7F7F7F:>] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:No swallow capacity limit (+ can swallow bosses)]
							[c/7F7F7F:> Stomach capacity:] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:{MiniCandyFairyStomachCapacity}]
							[c/7F7F7F:>] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Cannot be escaped]
							[c/7F7F7F:> Digestion tick damage:] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:{MiniCandyFairyDigestDamage}]
							[c/7F7F7F:> Digestion tick rate:] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:{MiniCandyFairyDigestRate}/sec]
							[c/7F7F7F:> Absorption rate:] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:{MiniCandyFairyAbsorbRate}/min]
							The Heiress [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:digests better] while a blood moon is out.
							[c/7F7F7F:> 1.5x digestion tick rate and absorption rate]
							The Heiress [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:digests much better] while the sun is out.
							[c/7F7F7F:> 2.0x digestion tick rate and absorption rate]
							The Heiress [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:digests better] while her escort is sleeping.
							[c/7F7F7F:> 1.25x digestion tick rate and absorption rate, also makes both scale with the speed of time]
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							The Empress always thought it very strange, the idea of having an heir to the throne in case she were rendered unfit to rule. The absolute AUDACITY of such a claim! Preposterous! She would quickly make a fool, and a fattening meal, of anyone that DARED to try and usurp her title!
							...though, as she slowly began to tutor a small prismatic fairy like herself by the name of Radianne, she began to see the value in having someone to eventually preside over, and voraciously devour the residents of, the Hallow with her. She would eat her if she tried to usurp the Empress, of course, but even a snack like her could be useful as an enforcer.

							With the Empress now dead (and/or digested), she now acts as your enforcer instead. She seeks to increase her brightness (and bulk, naturally) by devouring the brightest snacks she can swallow. Don't worry about her gut; she's eaten plenty of tough meals in the past.
							'''
					}
				}
			}

			AdhesiveBandage: {
				Short:
					'''
					Reduces the effects of Bleeding
					Slightly slows Softened buildup
					Won't hold up well to a gastric assault
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					While worn by a player:
					> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Grants immunity] to [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Bleeding].
					> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Slows Softened buildup by {AdhesiveBandageSoftenedBuildupReduction}].
					If this item runs out of durability via indirect digestion damage, it is immediately removed from your inventory and added to the stomach contents of your predator.
					'''
				Flavor: A simple adhesive bandage, meant to halt the flow of blood from open wounds to make it easier for them to heal. Medical practitioners carry a nigh-endless number of these.
			}

			HealthRegenAndPotionCooldownBand: {
				Short:
					'''
					Slightly boosts health regeneration and lowers max potion cooldown while worn
					Boosts health regeneration more, lowers max potion cooldown, and hastens potion cooldown while digesting
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					While worn by a player:
					> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{HealthRegenBandIIWornHealthRegen} HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Artificial)]
					> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Reduces the initial duration of Potion Sickness] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:25%].
					Upon running out of durability inside a player, until fully digested, and for 10 minutes thereafter:
					> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{HealthRegenBandIIEatenHealthRegen} HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Artificial)]
					> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Reduces the initial duration of Potion Sickness] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:25%].
					> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Potion Sickness wears off twice as fast].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					By combining a simple rejuvenating wristband and a magical stone imbued with life essence, you've managed to make: another wristband. That does the exact same thing.
					That said, it tastes better than either of its parts! Which is always a good reason to upgrade anything, frankly. Any upgrade that makes your gear a better snack for emergencies is a good upgrade.
					'''
			}

			ShimmerCloak:
				'''
				Grants immunity to Intangibility
				Hold <down> to temporarily bypass this immunity
				Allows you to safely drink shimmer
				'''
		}

