		Consumables: {
			Food: {
				ChickenNugget: {
					Short:
						'''
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
						'Definitely contains harpy'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
					Flavor:
						'''
						Often collectively called "chicken nuggets" for simplicity's sake, these nuggets of breaded, thoroughly-cooked meat actually come from a wide variety of birds and harpies alike.
						You'll most often find these in kids' meals in fast food chains, or on the young ones' section of the menu in restaurants; more mature folks generally prefer at least full limbs of well-prepared meat, if they're not swallowing the origin bird whole and alive.
						'''
				}

				ChocolateChipCookie: {
					Short:
						'''
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
						'New and mmmproved'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
					Flavor:
						'''
						One of the easiest cookie types to bake.
						The chocolate chips provide an undeniably sweet and delectable tint to the firm base of a normal cookie.
						Can be easily experimented with using additional ingredients to create even more delicious cookies.
						'''
				}

				Fries: {
					Short:
						'''
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
						'Hey, where's the ketchup?'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
					Flavor:
						'''
						One of the most common things to do with a potato is to carve it up into nice little sticks and fry them. The result, rather uncreatively, is called a batch of fries.
						Depending on where you find these in restaurants, they can be served with a wide variety of different other foods, such as fish or burgers.
						'''
				}

				GingerbreadCookie: {
					Short:
						'''
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
						'No plot armor this time, fuckboy'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
					Flavor:
						'''
						The easiest type of cookie to bake. Uses no captivating ingredients whatsoever.
						In old times, an extra ingredient added to these sorts of cookies would cause them to grow sentient, fleeing from their creators. Sveetian culture still cultivates this ingredient in controlled doses and allows these cookies a place of their own (with limitations), but elsewhere? They have nowhere to run with all the sweets-hungry predators around.
						This one represents one of the simplest and least nuanced cookies to be baked with that peculiar ingredient.
						'''
				}

				PotatoChips: {
					Short:
						'''
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
						'Also known as crisps'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
					Flavor:
						'''
						Not quite as common a culinary choice as fries, chips are still a frequently-utilized use case for potatoes in cooking.
						Generally much crispier and crunchier than fries, which lends well to seeing them offered as snacks in places where that crunchiness is preferred.
						'''
				}

				SugarCookie: {
					Short:
						'''
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
						'Not made with snow, surprisingly'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
					Flavor:
						'''
						A very common treat in Sveetia due to the commonplace nature of sugar as a cooking and baking ingredient.
						Provides plenty of energy to help get through the day in batches, or a quick pick-me-up as a lone snack.
						'''
				}
			}

			Potions: {
				Ale: {
					Short:
						'''
						Makes you tipsy while, and for a minute or two after, digesting
						While tipsy, you're better with melee combat and eating people; not as good with digesting them, though
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						It's alcohol in a mug. What do you want me to say?
						Lucky you, not only are glass mugs super easy to digest, but the booze will spill over the top as it goes down your throat, too, so you'll feel the effects right away.

						While in a stomach, until fully digested, and for 1 minute and 30 seconds thereafter, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:inflicts the Tipsy debuff].
						This buff improves your melee capabilities and internal capacities, at the cost of some defense and some digestion rates.
						'''
					Flavor: A simple glass of ale. Most drunkands would swallow mugs like these by the pound with ale still in them, or even drink the kegs dry directly. Sometimes, they'd even swallow down the kegs themselves!
				}

				Healing: {
					Lesser: {
						Short:
							'''
							Heals you for a small amount when drank
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							Heals you a small amount all at once when drank.
							Since you're just swallowing the whole bottle, with the cap still on, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
							You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

							Once the bottle breaks:
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:Heals] for [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{HealPotionLesserValue} HP].
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:Inflicts Potion Sickness] until fully digested, and for 60 seconds thereafter.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							Healing potions are an extremely common commodity all around the world; if you need something patched up, your best bet is to ask the local medical practitioner for a dosage of a potion!
							This one is unrefined; its recipe is rough, moreso a makeshift variant made by adventurers than anything professionally produced. Still, it can help heal your wounds in a pinch.
							'''
					}

					Normal: {
						Short:
							'''
							Heals you for a modest amount when drank
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							Heals you a modest amount all at once when drank.
							Since you're just swallowing the whole bottle, with the cap still on, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
							You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

							Once the bottle breaks:
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:Heals] for [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{HealPotionNormalValue} HP].
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:Inflicts Potion Sickness] until fully digested, and for 60 seconds thereafter.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							Healing potions are an extremely common commodity all around the world; if you need something patched up, your best bet is to ask the local medical practitioner for a dosage of a potion!
							This one is refined a bit; while not as impressive as more carefully-devised recipes, it is able to heal for quite a bit, able to patch up most small wounds effortlessly and slightly soothe the pains of larger ones.
							'''
					}

					Greater: {
						Short:
							'''
							Heals you for a large amount when drank
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							Heals you a large amount all at once when drank.
							Since you're just swallowing the whole bottle, with the cap still on, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
							You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

							Once the bottle breaks:
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:Heals] for [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{HealPotionGreaterValue} HP].
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:Inflicts Potion Sickness] until fully digested, and for 60 seconds thereafter.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							Healing potions are an extremely common commodity all around the world; if you need something patched up, your best bet is to ask the local medical practitioner for a dosage of a potion!
							This one's recipe is more naturally-based, and it is well-refined. Using its more naturally-inclined ingredients, it manages to heal for a great deal with little devaluing compared to its lesser counterparts.
							'''
					}

					Super: {
						Short:
							'''
							Heals you for a huge amount when drank
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							Heals you a huge amount all at once when drank.
							Since you're just swallowing the whole bottle, with the cap still on, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
							You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

							Once the bottle breaks:
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:Heals] for [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{HealPotionSuperValue} HP].
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:Inflicts Potion Sickness] until fully digested, and for 60 seconds thereafter.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							Healing potions are an extremely common commodity all around the world; if you need something patched up, your best bet is to ask the local medical practitioner for a dosage of a potion!
							This one reaches towards greatness; while perfection is inachievable, this potion manages to heal many of the more major wounds with but a single serving. The serving size? 1 potion!
							'''
					}
				}

				Ironskin: {
					Short:
						'''
						Provides increased defense while digesting
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						   
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Improves your body's ability to shrug off attacks, at least from the outside, when drank.
						Since you're just swallowing the whole bottle, with the cap still on, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
						You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

						Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 8 minutes thereafter:
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases defense] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{IronskinPotionDefenseValue}]. [c/7F7F7F:(Artificial)]
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						While consuming iron ore directly does not provide any noteworthy benefits, there are a number of ways to make it beneficial to consume.
						This potion does it by adding some additional natural ingredients typically found below the surface, bringing out the defensive nature of the metal.
						'''
				}

				Rage: {
					Short:
						'''
						Boosts crit chance and your ability to swallow new prey and finish churning old ones while digesting
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Improves your precision with your attacks and makes you better at getting down live prey and sloshing dead ones into cellulite when drank.
						Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
						You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

						Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter:
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases critical strike chance] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{RagePotionCritChanceBoost}].
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases GLP] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{RagePotionGLPBoost}].
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{RagePotionABSBoost}].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						An amateur-level potion fashioned from a bloody subspecies of piranha which makes its home in the sanguine seas of the Crimson.
						While digesting, it makes the consumer uncannily accurate with their shots and stomach, targeting weak points while shooting up, swallowing down, and sloshing all around (what's left of) their prey, regardless of whether that prey was once an ally or not.
						'''
				}

				Regeneration: {
					Short:
						'''
						Helps regenerate health while digesting
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Improves your body's ability to heal itself from injuries when drank.
						Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
						You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

						Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 6 minutes thereafter:
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{RegenPotionRegenFlat} HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Artificial)]
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						Simple beginner-level potions like this one are as commonplace as any other tech these days, being meant to help adventurers keep on their feet and off their fellows' waistlines.
						This one's in an easy-to-swallow bottle, and meant to help gradually patch up smaller injuries. Unfortunately for you, it probably won't save you from being churned up alive.
						'''
				}

				Sake: {
					Short:
						'''
						Makes you tipsy while, and for a short while after, digesting
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						It's alcohol, but fancy! And in a fancy bottle!
						Since you're just swallowing the whole bottle, with the cap still on, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
						As such, it may take a moment before you really start to feel the good vibes you're drinking this stuff for.

						Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:inflicts the Tipsy debuff].
						This buff improves your melee capabilities and internal capacities, at the cost of some defense and some digestion rates.
						'''
					Flavor: A well-made beverage from the heart of Turea, made predominantly for its endless lineages of princes and princesses...yet still marketed as a drink for the wealthy of other countries, and an exotic booze for those with a few currencies to spare.
				}

				Swiftness: {
					Short:
						'''
						Makes you feel lighter on your feet while digesting
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Allows you to move a bit quicker both with and without a full gut when drank.
						Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
						You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

						Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 8 minutes thereafter:
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases movement speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{SwiftnessPotionMoveSpeedBonus}].
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{SwiftnessPotionStomachWeightReduction}].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						A beginner-level potion mixed using the refreshing waters of a cactus and the sporadicity of blinkroot.
						While digesting, it tends towards making the consumer feel lighter on their feet, even with a full stomach.
						'''
				}

				Wrath: {
					Short:
						'''
						Boosts damage and your ability to quiet down your prey while digesting
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Improves the damage output of your swings, shots, and stomach alike when drank.
						Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
						You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

						Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter:
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{WrathPotionDamageBoost}].
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{WrathPotionTUMBoost}].
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases ACI] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{WrathPotionACIBoost}].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						An amateur-level potion fashioned from the oils of a spiteful fish which makes its home in pitch-dark purple Corrupted waters.
						While digesting, it makes the consumer rather angry, increasing their combat and predatory prowesses alike. An adventurer with this would-be curse could easily carve up and churn down their fellows into a healthy layer of fat just as easily as they could their foes.
						'''
				}

				WellFed: {
					Short:
						'''
						Minor improvements to all stats
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						The 'Well Fed' buff is based on a value between -3.5 and 3.5, multiplying the effect of the buff.
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases the Well Fed value] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{FedValue}].
						'''
					Flavor: "[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.White}:Minor improvements to all stats]"
				}

				WellFed2: {
					Short:
						'''
						Medium improvements to all stats
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						The 'Well Fed' buff is based on a value between -3.5 and 3.5, multiplying the effect of the buff.
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases the Well Fed value] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{FedValue}].
						'''
					Flavor: "[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.White}:Medium improvements to all stats]"
				}

				WellFed3: {
					Short:
						'''
						Major improvements to all stats
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						The 'Well Fed' buff is based on a value between -3.5 and 3.5, multiplying the effect of the buff.
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases the Well Fed value] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{FedValue}].
						'''
					Flavor: "[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.White}:Major improvements to all stats]"
				}
			}

			LifeCrystal: {
				Short:
					'''
					On use, the crystal is broken apart, providing a few revitalizing effects
					These effects also apply when it is eaten, and eating it provides additional bonuses
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					When eaten by anything:
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:Heals for {LifeCrystalEatHeal} health] instantly upon running out of durability.
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Grants the Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{LifeCrystalEatRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
					When used normally by a player OR upon running out of durability when eaten by a player:
					- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:increases maximum health] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:20].
					- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:1].
					  - The above two bonuses can stack for up to {LifeCrystalsMax} crystals used/eaten.
					- If you have reached 15 Life Crystals used/eaten, permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:mitigates the impact of stomach weight] by {MaxLifeCrystalsPermaWeightReduction}x.
					Life Crystals used/eaten by this character (max. {LifeCrystalsMax}): [c/{LifeCrystalsUsedColor}:{LifeCrystalsUsed}].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A mysterious crystal which forms in the deeper caverns of Terraria, drawing in all manner of adventurers, curious and craving alike, to examine it. Upon breaking one apart, either via pure force or prolonged exposure to a gastric gauntlet of digestion, the crystal fires off a spell which lends its power to the user/consumer, greatly increasing their vitality...though part of the effect only occurs up to a certain number of times. The exact science behind this spell is poorly understood, but has led many to believe a powerful being created these crystals with the intention of letting them be eaten by worldly creatures in need of strength to hunt. While this was initially thought to be an unfounded claim, the fact that powerful predators have caught truly unnaturally perfect prey in the past suggests otherwise...
					Those who have eaten Life Crystals before note that doing so feels a lot like eating rock candy, with a notable cherry-like flavor. The first person to do it ended up famous worldwide for quite some time because of a number of hilariously inept, yet somehow successful achievements. A pity he ended up getting gulped down and gurgled by a gleeful, gluttonous ghost.
					'''
			}

			LifeFruit: {
				Short:
					'''
					Provides a swathe of truly revitalizing effects when eaten
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					When eaten by anything:
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:Heals for {LifeFruitEatHeal} health] instantly upon running out of durability.
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Grants the Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{LifeFruitEatRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
					When eaten by a player who has eaten at least 15 Life Crystals, upon running out of durability:
					- Permanently [c/{LifeFruitHealthBonusColor}:increases maximum health by 5].
					- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{LifeFruitStomachStrengthBonus}].
					- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:increases ACI] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{LifeFruitAcidStrengthBonus}].
					  - The above three bonuses can stack up to {LifeFruitMax} times.
					Life Fruit eaten by this character (max. {LifeFruitMax}): [c/{LifeFruitUsedColor}:{LifeFruitUsed}].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A mysterious crop only ever found in the depths of a specific jungle on Terraria, this delectable fruit seems like only a rare delicacy at first...but when sufficient residual mana sourced from Life Crystals' magic swirls within the body of the consumer, it bestows upon them and their stomach greater power than a Life Crystal ever could. Many have speculated these were coerced into growing in much the same way that Life Crystals are thought to have been...and given that angels from a plane beyond have documentedly visited our planet and even been eaten by particularly ambitious predators on it, this isn't such an outlandish claim.
					While rather few have managed to taste the fruit in full, due to a certain trio of feminine floral demis deep in the jungle craving them and those who would seek out their craved snacks at all times, those who have managed to gulp down these fruits have reported a pleasant and tasteful combination of orange and mango flavors as the main appeal of the Life Fruit as an exotic snack option.
					'''
			}

			ManaCrystal: {
				Short:
					'''
					On use, the crystal is broken apart, providing a few magically beneficial effects
					These effects also apply when it is eaten, and eating it provides additional bonuses
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					When eaten by anything:
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ManaHeal}:Restores 100 mana] instantly upon running out of durability.
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Grants the Mana Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{ManaCrystalEatManaRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
					When used normally by a player OR upon running out of durability when eaten by a player:
					- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ManaHeal}:increases maximum mana] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:20].
					- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:increases the ABS stat] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:1].
					  - The above two bonuses can stack for up to {ManaCrystalsMax} crystals used/eaten.
					Mana Crystals used/eaten by this character (max. {ManaCrystalsMax}): [c/{ManaCrystalsUsedColor}:{ManaCrystalsUsed}].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					Very commonly made and just as commonly munched on, these oversized star-shaped batches of blue-raspberry-flavored rock candy are infused with residual mana from pieces of the stars above, making them readily provide those who eat them with additional space in their mana reserves and an easier time processing meals that have fallen still into more mana for said reserves.
					Many have speculated that there could be less eating-oriented approaches to using these, but why would you care about that when you can munch on such a big batch of blue-raspberry-flavored rock candy?

					...and then someone proved why it could be a bad idea to overspecialize, so now the spell also fires off if the rock candy is broken apart.
					'''
			}
		}

		Currency: {
			Coins: {
				Generic: {
					Short: Can be used in shops
					Long:
						'''
						Coins in your inventory will [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:auto-convert to highest denominations] whenever possible.
						Can be used as currency in most shops.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						of a currency long since abandoned by most countries.
						However, those who travel the space between those countries still find it useful to use it for trades with people who live in the wilder regions of Terraria.
						'''
				}

				CopperCoin: {
					Short:
						'''
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Short}
						'Not made of chocolate, sadly'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Used as the lowest denomination of "universal" currency.
						100 of these have equal value to a [i:SilverCoin] Silver Coin.
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Long}
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						The lowest denomination {$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Flavor}
						These are often treated as little more than individual bites of cereal in most areas, these are often doomed in massive amounts to the gut of anything, and anyone, that wants to churn them into gut fat.
						Roughly equal in value to:
						- Avarsici: Favor.
						- Sveetia: [c/FFAFAF:Too low value.]
						- Turea: N/A.
						- Desperais: N/A.
						'''
				}

				SilverCoin: {
					Short:
						'''
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Short}
						'Also not made of chocolate, also sadly'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Used as the second-lowest denomination of "universal" currency.
						1 of these has equal value to 100 [i:CopperCoin] Copper Coins.
						100 of these have equal value to 1 [i:GoldCoin] Gold Coin.
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Long}
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						The second-lowest denomination {$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Flavor}
						Snacking on these is fairly common against those who can make a comfortable living elsewise, though you won't find those with lower-paying jobs doing so...very much.
						Roughly equal in value to:
						- Avarsici: 1 Mark.
						- Sveetia: [c/FFAFAF:Too low value for conversion.]
						- Turea: N/A.
						- Desperais: N/A.
						'''
				}

				GoldCoin: {
					Short:
						'''
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Short}
						'Voted 'Most Likely To Be Made Of Chocolate'!...but it isn't'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Used as the second-highest denomination of "universal" currency.
						1 of these has equal value to 100 [i:SilverCoin] Silver Coins.
						100 of these have equal value to 1 [i:PlatinumCoin] Platinum Coin.
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Long}
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						The second-highest denomination {$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Flavor}
						Snacking on these usually means you're fairly wealthy, being able to doom at your leisure small swathes of your riches to a fate even better than your bank account: bulking up your backside.
						Roughly equal in value to:
						- Avarsici: 1 Great Mark.
						- Sveetia: 4 Sugar Sterlings.
						- Turea: N/A.
						- Desperais: N/A.
						'''
				}

				PlatinumCoin: {
					Short:
						'''
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Short}
						'Still need to know if it's made of chocolate? Are you just that eager to gurgle all your wealth into a wealth of belly fat?'

						'...because it's not made of chocolate'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Used as the second-highest denomination of "universal" currency.
						1 of these has equal value to 100 [i:GoldCoin] Gold Coins.
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Long}
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						The highest denomination {$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Flavor}
						Snacking on these generally denotes someone of extremely high value --- such high value that even the best denomination of currency is naught but pleasant cereal to them.
						Alternatively, some lower-class may swallow individual coins of this caliber for the experience --- there is a certain exotic rush that comes with swallowing something worth a small fortune like a mere snack, digesting it into naught but a few more calories or a bit of belly fat, and having the only evidence it was ever there be a pleasant little belch that rises from your belly.
						Roughly equal in value to:
						- Avarsici: 1 Grand Mark.
						- Sveetia: 400 Sugar Sterlings.
						- Turea: N/A. Turean folk trade in material (or living) possessions, not petty currency.
						- Desperais: N/A. People pay, and charge, in good, meaty, fighty food around those parts.
						'''
				}
			}
		}

		Placeables: {
			Bars: {
				Copper: {
					Short:
						'''
						A very sweet-tasting "gem"
						'Pretty sappy, if you ask me'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long: Can be found commonly [c:]
					Flavor:
						'''
						Many people in old times assumed this was a gemstone. It's not! It's actually fossilized tree sap which found a home in desert regions, nestling in the remains of creatures from ages past.
						While it IS possible to create amber through fairly simple means, most of these means have subsequently been heavily commercialized and privatized by the desserts industry. Why? It's simple!

						Amber tastes very sweet. Sweet-tasting things are desserts to be enjoyed! And where there are desserts to be enjoyed...there's ALWAYS money to be made.
						'''
				}
			}

			Gems: {
				Amber: {
					Short:
						'''
						A very sweet-tasting "gem"
						'Pretty sappy, if you ask me'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Can be found sometimes within the desert, either on its own or when extracted from [i:3347] Desert Fossils.
						Can be used to fashion a select assortment of desert-related items.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						Many people in old times assumed this was a gemstone. It's not! It's actually fossilized tree sap which found a home in desert regions, nestling in the remains of creatures from ages past.
						While it IS possible to create amber through fairly simple means, most of these means have subsequently been heavily commercialized and privatized by the desserts industry. Why? It's simple!

						Amber tastes very sweet. Sweet-tasting things are desserts to be enjoyed! And where there are sweet-tasting desserts to be enjoyed...there's ALWAYS money to be made.
						'''
				}

				Amethyst: {
					Short:
						'''
						A rather common gemstone
						'Conducts mischief, predominantly'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Found fairly commonly in the caves of the world.
						Can be used to fashion assorted early-game items.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						A common gemstone such as amethyst can be found in virtually any cave that travels subsurface, though the purple hues of this one give off a certain...vibe.
						Amethysts are most typically used as conduits for the abilities of shapeshifters to be more easily controlled, amongst other mischievous use cases.
						'''
				}

				Diamond: {
					Short:
						'''
						A valuable, rare gemstone
						'Chromatic diversity is so last setting'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Found rarely in the deeper (accessible) layers of the world.
						Highly valuable, or at least used to be. Could sell for a lot of money.
						Can be used to fashion assorted powerful early-game items.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						Oftentimes mistakenly assumed to be the hardest gem in existence, formed in the deep layers of Terraria's crust as the result of ages of time and temperament. However, in more recent times, alongside the view of a natural set of four as an omen from worlds beyond being proven false, even tougher gems have been found and even forged with modern life's own means.
						While technology --- both magical and electrical entwined --- has advanced enough to create these gems decently reliably, naturally-formed diamonds are still a valuable commodity, as artificially-compressed diamonds carry traces of other materials and thus have substantially lower purity.
						Swallowing one isn't recommended, as it is by far the toughest gem to digest due to its sheer hardness...but if you can, having a large enough diamond for dinner is said to make your body much sturdier, inside and out.
						'''
				}

				Emerald: {
					Short:
						'''
						A fairly valuable and rare gem
						'Conducts...focus? Is focus a quantifiable metric?'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Found fairly rarely in the deeper (accessible) layers of the world.
						Valuable. Could sell for a decent amount of money.
						Can be used to fashion assorted accuracy-boosting early-game items.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						A fairly rare gemstone colored a precise, hungering green.
						Emeralds are gemstones often attributed to the likes of ranged weapon enthusiasts, its shine when held to light almost resembling the predatory glint in a storied archer's eye when they spot their latest prey.
						Swallowing one often isn't recommended due to its hardness, but if you can, having a large enough emerald for dinner is said to improve your eyesight, and thus, your accuracy for the shots and snacks  that matter.
						'''
				}

				Ruby: {
					Short:
						'''
						A fairly valuable and rare gem
						'Conducts heat'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Found rarely in the deeper (accessible) layers of the world.
						Highly valuable, or at least used to be. Could sell for a lot of money.
						Can be used to fashion assorted strength-boosting early-game items.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						A fairly rare gemstone colored a pleasantly warm red.
						Rubies are very common gems to find in any gear suited to a brawler, as they're often said to represent the fire inside of the fighter's heart (and stomach).
						Swallowing one often isn't recommended due to its hardness, but if you can, having a large enough ruby for dinner is said to make you and your stomach pack a bigger punch.
						'''
				}

				Sapphire: {
					Short:
						'''
						A fairly valuable and rare gem
						'Conducts mana'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Found rarely in the deeper (accessible) layers of the world.
						Highly valuable, or at least used to be. Could sell for a lot of money.
						Can be used to fashion assorted magical early-game items.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						A fairly rare gemstone, colored a pleasantly dark blue.
						Sapphires are very common gems to find in any gear suited to a mage or adjacent, as they tend to conduct mana the best out of all gemstones.
						Swallowing one often isn't recommended due to its hardness, but if you can, having a large enough sapphire for dinner is said to make you smarter.
						'''
				}

				Topaz: {
					Short:
						'''
						A rather common gemstone
						'The lamest of them, too'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Found very commonly in caves that travel beneath the surface.
						Can be used to fashion assorted (not very powerful) early-game items.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						Easily one of the most common and, not coincidentally, most lame gemstones ever discovered on Terraria.
						Can make for a good snack in a pinch, though it can be tough to digest without a strong system.
						'''
				}
			}
		}

		Weapons: {
			Melee: {
				BorealWoodSword: {
					Short:
						'''
						Can be swung to deal damage
						May be unwieldy in tighter stomachs
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] to swing the sword, dealing [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:100% damage] to struck targets.
						Cannot be swung in a stomach which has less than {BroadswordSwingCapacityMin} max capacity.
						When successfully swung in a stomach, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:deals struggle damage] instead.
						Effectiveness is reduced if not done to the beat of the current pred's struggle chart.
						'''
					Flavor: A simple sword fashioned from boreal wood. Has a chilly aftertaste resembling the taste of snow.
				}

				CactusSword: {
					Short:
						'''
						Hurts your throat a noteworthy bit to swallow
						While digesting, enemies that hit you take damage themselves
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:Deals {CactusSwordSwallowDamage} damage to the pred] when swallowed.
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:Inflicts {$Mods.V2.StatusEffects.Voraria.Debuffs.SoreThroat.Name} for {CactusSwordSoreThroatTime} seconds] when swallowed.
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Grants the Thorns buff] while digesting, and for [c/FFFF7F:{CactusSwordThornsTime} seconds] longer once fully digested.
						'''
					Flavor: A dubiously-wieldy sword fashioned from cactus cuttings. While its prickly nature makes it fairly usable as a weapon, one has to wonder how it would taste...and if there's any way to get around the discomforting amount of spines it still has.
				}

				CopperShortsword: {
					Short:
						'''
						Can be thrust to deal damage
						Freely usable, even in tighter stomachs
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] to thrust the sword forward, dealing [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:100% damage] to struck targets.
						Can be used normally inside any stomach to [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:deal struggle damage] to a pred.
						Effectiveness is reduced if not done to the beat of the current pred's struggle chart.
						'''
					Flavor: A shortsword forged from copper. While its power isn't anything to write home about, it can still prove an effective weapon in a pinch.
				}

				FruitcakeChakram: {
					Short:
						'''
						Throw it to get it as far away from yourself as possible; alternatively, you can eat it
						No matter how angry eating it makes you, it is unfortunately the best way to rid the world of this menace
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:Deals {FruitcakeChakramSwallowDamage} damage to the pred] when swallowed, because it just tastes that bad.
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:Inflicts {$Mods.V2.StatusEffects.Voraria.Debuffs.SoreThroat.Name} for {FruitcakeChakramSoreThroatTime} seconds] when swallowed; see above
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:Inflicts the Poison debuff] while in your stomach, and for [c/FFFF7F:{FruitcakeChakramPoisonTime} seconds] longer once fully digested; see above.
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Grants the Wrath buff] while in your stomach, and for [c/FFFF7F:{FruitcakeChakramWrathTime} seconds] longer once fully digested, because needing to eat this thing makes one VERY angry.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						A single look at this abominable crime against catering makes you wonder if it was ever supposed to be food in the first place. The mere THOUGHT of gracing this...THING with death by digestion almost seems too good a mercy for it.

						You're not alone in that assessment, either. Fruitcake was first made long ago by a rather...eccentric baker in a territory previously owned by one of the many, MANY royals that have made their mark on Terraria over the years.

						It is now banned within any and all Avarsician borders; the very kingdom whose then-prince Markus Caldera originally annexed the country (and its queen) as a way to prove his worth (and, to his credit, he WAS successful on both fronts) as heir to the throne.
						The Apex Convocation unanimously agreed to ban it from Desperais, and despite the hundreds of years and countless shifts in the seat fillings that have passed since that initial ruling, that ban has never been lifted.
						Countless other territories outside of these two notable powers also ban it, and only ever for one reason: the mere existence of this concept is slander against the good name of bakers the planet over.

						The only use this has is as a weapon, and POTENTIALLY as emergency rations if all else is gone.
						'''
				}

				RichMahoganySword: {
					Short:
						'''
						Can be swung to deal damage
						May be unwieldy in tighter stomachs
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] to swing the sword, dealing [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:100% damage] to struck targets.
						Cannot be swung in a stomach which has less than {BroadswordSwingCapacityMin} max capacity.
						When successfully swung in a stomach, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:deals struggle damage] instead.
						Effectiveness is reduced if not done to the beat of the current pred's struggle chart.
						'''
					Flavor: A simple sword fashioned from rich mahogany wood. The aftertaste reminds you of the jungle's plant life.
				}

				OakWoodSword: {
					Short:
						'''
						Can be swung to deal damage
						May be unwieldy in tighter stomachs
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] to swing the sword, dealing [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:100% damage] to struck targets.
						Cannot be swung in a stomach which has less than {BroadswordSwingCapacityMin} max capacity.
						When successfully swung in a stomach, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:deals struggle damage] instead.
						Effectiveness is reduced if not done to the beat of the current pred's struggle chart.
						'''
					Flavor: A simple sword fashioned from oak wood, and tasting about the same.
				}
			}

			Ranged: {
				BorealWoodBow: {
					Short:
						'''
						Can fire arrows to deal damage
						Incredibly unwieldy in all but the roomiest bellies
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] to shoot an arrow, dealing [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:100% damage] to the first target it hits.
						Some arrows may have [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:special properties]; examine these in the tooltips of your arrows.
						Cannot be used in any stomach with less than 20.0 capacity or attached to a pred of a base size lower than 4.0.
						When successfully fired in a stomach, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:deals struggle damage] instead.
						Effectiveness is reduced if not done to the beat of the current pred's struggle chart.
						'''
					Flavor: A simple bow fashioned from boreal wood. It has a chilly aftertaste resembling the taste of snow.
				}

				OakWoodBow: {
					Short:
						'''
						Can fire arrows to deal damage
						Incredibly unwieldy in all but the roomiest bellies
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] to shoot an arrow, dealing [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:100% damage] to the first target it hits.
						Some arrows may have [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:special properties]; examine these in the tooltips of your arrows.
						Cannot be used in any stomach with less than 20.0 capacity or attached to a pred of a base size lower than 4.0.
						When successfully fired in a stomach, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:deals struggle damage] instead.
						Effectiveness is reduced if not done to the beat of the current pred's struggle chart.
						'''
					Flavor: A simple bow fashioned from oak wood, and tasting about the same.
				}

				FlareGun: {
					Short:
						'''
						Can fire flares to deal damage; must be reloaded between shots
						Light and easy to use in a belly
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] to shoot a flare, dealing [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:{FlareGunDamageRatio} damage] to the first target it hits.
						Some flares may have [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:special properties]; examine these in the tooltips of your flares.

						Can only fire a flare if said flare is loaded into the barrel.
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Right-click] to begin loading a flare into the barrel. This takes {FlareGunReloadTime} seconds.
						Only one flare can be loaded into the barrel at a time.

						Can be used in any stomach.
						When successfully fired in a stomach, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:deals struggle damage] instead.
						Effectiveness is reduced if not done to the beat of the current pred's struggle chart.
						Deals [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:+{FlareGunNonBurnproofBonus} damage] against the stomachs of preds which are not burnproof. Deals [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:no damage] against those of preds who are.
						'''
					Flavor: While sadly not used much in the well-respected profession of hunting compared to other ranged weapons of its caliber, flare guns are a common tool amongst adventurers and spelunkers alike to mark important locations or raise visibility in dark caves. The gun's design marks it as predominantly for usage outside of a stomach...but that doesn't make it a bad queasing weapon in a pinch, so long as you have flares left undigested to load it with.
				}
			}
		}

		Feather: {
			Short:
				'''
				'Don't pluck me! They went thataway!'
				{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
				'''
			Long:
				'''
				Can be used to craft certain wing types.
				Can be used as a potion ingredient.
				'''
			Flavor:
				'''
				A simple feather plucked from the wing of a hungry harpy.
				These feathers are often arranged in fashions that promote easy targeted flight, allowing the greedy birds in the sky to swoop down and scoop up their kicky, shouty prey with ease.
				'''
		}

		Gel: {
			Short:
				'''
				Was a part of a gelatinous creature. It's bouncy!
				{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
				'''
			Long:
				'''
				Gel is used by the gelatinous creatures in the Terrarian world. 
				If this piece of gel is alive or not is not easy to determine, but you can swallow it with ease. Quite tasty too.
				'''
			Flavor: Tastes similar to sweet jelly, and closer to a berry - similar to Blueberries!
		}

		Cobweb: {
			Short:
				'''
				'Nature's cotton candy'
				{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
				'''
			Long:
				'''
				Can be used to craft silk at a loom.
				Can also be used alongside bones to craft some gear.
				'''
			Flavor: It... might taste good? I've never eaten cobwebs myself so i can't confirm.
		}
	}

	Voraria: {
		Armor: {
			CloverArmorSetBonus: 7 defense, drastically increased struggling strength
			FungalFairySetBonus: Enables eating regular projectiles, automatically eat projectiles that are about to hit you

			CloverHeadAccessories: {
				Short:
					'''
					7% increased critical strike chance
					Increased maximum prey swallowing size and struggling strength
					Slightly increased luck
					'Three head accessories in one slot? Is that even legal?'
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases critical strike chance] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:7%].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases luck] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:0.3].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases GLP] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:5].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases struggle strength] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:75%].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					Clover's choice of headwear. It is an amalgamation of items stuffed into a single slot.
					It consists of:
					- A four-leaf clover hair... hatpin?
					- An awfully bright tophat.
					- 'Felt Goggles', despite not actually being made of felt.
					At first, Clover didn't actually like green that much, but eventually it grew on her.
					'''
			}

			CloverSweater: {
				Short:
					'''
					7% increased critical strike chance
					Increased struggle strength
					Increased stomach capacity, struggling strength and food absorption rate
					Slightly increased luck
					'It's awfully comfortable. You could probably fall asleep standing just by wearing this...'
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases critical strike chance] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:7%].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases luck] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:0.1].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:8].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:6].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases struggle strength] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:100%].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					One of Clover's many sweaters. It is pretty large for both you and her.
					It is RIDICULOUS how soft and comfortable this thing is.
					You'd think it's like, enchanted or somethi- OH WAIT it is.
					'''
			}

			CloverStockings: {
				Short:
					'''
					7% increased critical strike chance
					20% increased movement speed
					Increased struggling strength
					Lowers stomach weight
					Slightly increased luck
					'They're more like thigh high socks, honestly.'
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases critical strike chance] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:7%].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases luck] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:0.1].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases movement speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:20%].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:15%].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases struggle strength] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:75%].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					It's a pair of Clover's stockings!
					...uh, what do you want me to say about this
					they're just enchanted socks
					like
					dude
					'''
			}

			MushroomHairpin: {
				Short:
					'''
					Increased maximum prey swallowing size and food absorption rate
					Increases your max number of minions by 1
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases GLP] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:7].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:7].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases your maximum number of minions] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:1].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A small hairpin which seems more akin to a cute, tiny glowing mushroom than an actual hairpin.
					You can't help but wonder if it'd start growing more on your head if you were to wear it long enough.
					'''
			}

			FungalDress: {
				Short:
					'''
					Increased stomach size
					Lowers stomach weight
					Increases your max number of minions by 1
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:9].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:20%].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A dress sewn from threads spun from glowing mushrooms and the other flora of the caves in which they're found.
					It's a bit tight. You'd think that fairies known for becoming Really Fucking Fat(TM) would make stretchier clothes, but alas...
					'''
			}

			ShroomiteHairpin: {
				Short:
					'''
					Increased maximum prey swallowing size, food absorption rate and acid strength
					Increases your max number of minions by 3
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases GLP] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:19].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:19].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases ACI] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:6].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases your maximum number of minions] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:3].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A small hairpin which seems more akin to a cute, tiny glowing mushroom than an actual hairpin.
					You can't help but wonder if it'd start growing more on your head if you were to wear it long enough.

					The catch is that this one, which is covered in shroomite, cannot. It will, however, eventually consume that shroomite and start growing anyway.
					'''
			}

			ShroomiteDress: {
				Short:
					'''
					Increased stomach size and acid strength
					Lowers stomach weight
					Increases your max number of minions by 2
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:22].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases ACI] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:6].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:40%].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases your maximum number of minions] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:2].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A large fungal fairy dress, now well-reinforced with shroomite and similar stronger materials.
					You had all the right materials to make it bigger, and yet... It's still small. Are you into this, or..?
					'''
			}
		}

		CheatItems: {
			RoseFlower: {
				Short:
					'''
					Gives you the same predatory prowess that Rose has, at no cost whatsoever
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					While worn, provides a number of extremely- and outright unfairly-beneficial predatorily-centric effects:
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Makes your stomach weightless, no matter what or who is in it.]
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Grants infinite swallow and stomach capacity, and makes it impossible for prey to escape your stomach unless you regurgitate them.]
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Grants the ability to eat bosses regardless of whether your currently-selected gear and abilities would allow you to.]
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Raises your acid tier to MILES beyond the maximum.]
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases digestion tick rate by a factor of 4.]
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases absorption rate by a factor of 8.]
					Several item effects and UI elements will be modified while this item or any of its counterparts are equipped.
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:this is a prefabricated copy of Rose's personal flower hairpin]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:it's not where any of her more				egregious predatory abilities come from]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:she is naturally just that much a glutton. ate an entire mountain range as a snack once]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:she tells people that this flower was the very last thing left from the last world she ate]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:she doesn't tell them that I made it for her when I made her]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:I made a virtually-infinite number of 'em so that if she accidentally ate it]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:(and she has, more times than I care to count)]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:she'd have another rarin' to go shortly thereafter to keep her happy]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:she tells me these flowers are delicious]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:then again, she thinks everything's delicious, so maybe take her word with a grain of salt]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:don't try to eat it. she'll know, and she'll make you a meal]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:no matter how strong you are or how invincible you think you are]

					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:after all, she REALLY likes the taste of these flowers]
					'''
			}

			VenomDevItem: {
				Short:
					'''
					Gives you the same predatory prowess that Venomizeous has, at no cost whatsoever
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					While worn, provides a number of extremely- and outright unfairly-beneficial predatorily-centric effects:
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Makes your stomach weightless, no matter what or who is in it.]
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Grants infinite swallow and stomach capacity, and makes it impossible for prey to escape your stomach unless you regurgitate them.]
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Grants the ability to eat bosses regardless of whether your currently-selected gear and abilities would allow you to.]
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Raises your acid tier to MILES beyond the maximum.]
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases digestion tick rate by a factor of 4.]
					[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases absorption rate by a factor of 8.]
					Several item effects and UI elements will be modified while this item or any of its counterparts are equipped.
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.VenomCommentary}:Venomizeous being a slim, fit vampire may make one think that they're no predator]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.VenomCommentary}:and that the slim and fit body would not even be able to fit a single casually sized prey.]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.VenomCommentary}:But don't let the size fool any predator or prey.]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.VenomCommentary}:Venomizeous being the glutton he is, will really consume anything.]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.VenomCommentary}:Be it a anything from small snacks to universe-sized meals, they]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.VenomCommentary}:somehow always have capacity for more.]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.VenomCommentary}:Venomizous who has devoured a large set of both small and large meals.]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.VenomCommentary}:Will still have the belly occasionally groan and gurgle for even more.]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.VenomCommentary}:What puts a stop to them is laziness, like any other predator perhaps.]
					
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.VenomCommentary}:This flower is watered with Venomizeous' own tears.]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.VenomCommentary}:Which somehow provides the same predatory capabilities that Venomizeous posses.]
					'''
			}

			SecondBestAngelFeather: {
				Short:
					'''
					Gives you St. Promethia's blessing to cram yourself into anyone you please
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long: "[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Allows you to get eaten by (be it naturally or by climbing into) anything that is able to eat people, even if it couldn't fit you otherwise.]"
				Flavor:
					'''
					A single feather from the one and only St. Promethia Hypate, an angelic gut slut who'd love nothing more than to see herself melted down into flab for every last predator on the planet and off of it --- even those that one would assume are unable to eat her.
					This is one of her favorite feathers, churned down into padding endless times, yet still as fresh as the day she was born. Simply holding it makes you feel like you haven't seen nearly enough of the innumerable predators of the world.
					'''
			}

			ServerMessageRelay: {
				Short:
					'''
					Allows a certain someone to speak directly into your world
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long: When kept in Rose's inventory, allows the [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:/authormessage] command to work.
				Flavor: "[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ThomasCommentary}:hi :>]"
			}
		}

		Accessories: {
			Thingymajigs: {
				Blank: {
					Short:
						'''
						Can be crafted into special accessories that can provide stat boosts
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long: This item does nothing on its own; instead, it is used to craft a variety of stat boosting accessories which can additionally be digested for small but permanent boosts.
					Flavor:
						'''
						One of Clover's strange creations.
						It is a fragment of unknown energy, waiting for the right conditions to be awakened.
						'''
				}

				Crimson: {
					Short:
						'''
						Increases damage and digestion damage
						Reduces max stomachache
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Dmg}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Dig}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:Decreases max stomachache] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Ache}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently increases digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PermDig}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear a faint heartbeat, and...something else. The sound sickens you.
						'''
				}

				Corruption: {
					Short:
						'''
						Increases damage and max stomachache
						Reduces digestion damage
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Dmg}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases max stomachache] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Ache}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:Decreases digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Dig}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently increases max stomachache] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PermAche}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear something splat onto a surface, and the flickering of an unnatural fire.
						'''
				}

				Desert: {
					Short:
						'''
						Increases struggle damage
						Decreases max stomachache
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases struggle damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Str}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:Decreases max stomachache] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Ache}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently increases struggle damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PermStr}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear a loud 'ow!', as if from someone getting pricked by a cactus.
						'''
				}

				Dungeon: {
					Short:
						'''
						Increases acid strength and max stomachache
						Reduces damage taken and stomach capacity
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Reduces damage taken] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Endu}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Dig}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases max stomachache] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Ache}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:Decreases stomach capacity] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Cap}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Permanently increases defense] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PermDef}].
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently increases max stomachache] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PermAche}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear what can only be described as a rave. What the shit? Do they, like. Party all the time there, and stop IMMEDIATELY when you get close? Bullshit.
						'''
				}

				Forest: {
					Short:
						'''
						Increases swallow capacity and food absorption rate
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases swallow capacity] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Buff}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases food absorption rate] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Buff}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently increases swallow capacity] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Perm}%].
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently increases prey absorption rate] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Perm}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear the wind grazing, and the chirping of birds yet to eat the early worms (and lamia).
						'''
				}

				Hallow: {
					Short:
						'''
						Increases movement speed and prey absorption rate
						Reduces max stomachache
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases movement speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Spd}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases prey absorption rate] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Abs}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:Decreases max stomachache] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Ache}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Permanently increases movement speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PermSpd}%].
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently increases prey absorption rate] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PermAbs}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear a double rainbow. You don't actually know what that'd sound like, or if rainbows even make sound at all...though the faint rumbling and gurgling coming from somewhere within the double rainbow gives you an idea of how it became one.
						'''
				}

				Jungle: {
					Short:
						'''
						Increases stomach capacity
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases stomach capacity] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Cap}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently increases stomach capacity] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PermCap}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear bees buzzing, and honey flowing through combs. At least one of the bees is also full of...something, though you can't make out what or who via sound alone.
						'''
				}

				Mushroom: {
					Short:
						'''
						Decreases body weight
						Increases stomach weight
						Increases stomach capacity based on how fat you are
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases body weight by] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{BWeight}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:Increases stomach weight by] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{SWeight}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases stomach capacity] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:1/4th of your extra body weight].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently decreases body weight by] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PermBWeight}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear funky beats.
						'''
				}

				Ocean: {
					Short:
						'''
						Requires wearer to be submerged in water or honey
						Increases digestion damage and prey absorption rate
						Decreases damage taken
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						If you [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:aren't submerged in water or honey], [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:this accessory will have no effect].
						The [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Wet] debuff and [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Honey] buff count for this accessory.
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Stat}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases prey absorption rate] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Stat}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Decreases damage taken] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Endu}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Perm}%].
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases prey absorption rate] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Perm}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear the ocean's waves, intermingling with thoroughly-muffled burbling and gurgling from the depths below them.
						'''
				}

				Shimmer: {
					Short:
						'''
						Increases swallow capacity, stomach capacity, acid strength and prey absorption rate
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases swallow capacity, stomach capacity, digestion damage and prey absorption rate] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Stat}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently increases GLP, TUM, ACI & ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Perm}].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear "Terraria 1.4.4 OST - 'Aether'".

						...wait, how do you even know what that is? Like, from an in-universe perspective?
						'''
				}

				Sky: {
					Short:
						'''
						Increases flight time
						Decreases stomach and body weight
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases flight time] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Wing}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Stat}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases body weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Stat}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Perm}%].
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases body weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Perm}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear tinnitus. And the rumbling of clouds, but mainly tinnitus.
						'''
				}

				Snow: {
					Short:
						'''
						Increases max stomachache
						Decreases struggle damage
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases max stomachache] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Ache}%].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:Decreases struggle damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Str}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently increases max stomachache] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PermAche}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear someone slip and fall on their ass. Evidently, said ass wasn't very big, judging from the impact sound.
						'''
				}

				Underworld: {
					Short:
						'''
						Increases acid strength
						If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to these effects
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Dig}%].
						When eaten:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently increases digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PermDig}%].
						This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						You listen close...

						...you hear lava bubbling, and demonfolk laughing and belching as they share a conversation you can't make out. How much of the lava is bubbling away in their bellies rather than outside of them is uncertain.
						'''
				}
			}

			Informational: {
				MealSizeScanner: {
					Short:
						'''
						Shows the size of nearby snacks, and helps you know if you're able to make them your next meals
						Functions from the inventory as well as normal accessory slots
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Most things that you can eat [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:display their size as a meal below themselves].
						If their size number is [c/00FF00:green], you are able to swallow them with ease.
						[c/7F7F7F:This means that your target meal would fit in your stomach normally, and nothing is keeping you from gobbling them up on sight. Go indulge a little!]
						If their size number is [c/FFFF00:yellow], you are able to swallow them, but might have a bit of trouble keeping them down or properly mulching them.
						[c/7F7F7F:This means that while your target meal would fit in your stomach normally, one of the following is true:]
						[c/7F7F7F:> Your stomach is too full to fit them due to other meals already inside it]
						[c/7F7F7F:> Your target meal's defense exceeds your stomach's digestion tick damage]
						[c/7F7F7F:> Your target meal's health exceeds 1 minute of your stomach's final DDPS (digestion damage per second, factors in defense)]
						[c/7F7F7F:> Your target meal's acid resist level exceeds your stomach's acid tier]
						If their size number is [c/FF0000:red], you aren't able to gulp and gurgle them into gut fat yet.
						[c/7F7F7F:This means that your target meal wouldn't fit in you due to your throat and/or stomach capacity being too low.]
						[c/7F7F7F:If this is the case, try to increase your GLP and TUM stats by whatever means you find throughout the game!]
						Functions from the inventory as well as when equipped in normal accessory slots.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						This peculiar device was originally designed for use by a mechanic to ensure optimal fullness-to-caloric-value weighting when consuming nearby living creatures and converting them into (potential) energy.
						It can do the same for you, if you care to, though its main use will almost certainly be making sure your eyes don't get bigger than your stomach...and/or throat.
						'''
				}

				PredCapacityScanner: {
					Short:
						'''
						Shows the stomach capacity of nearby entities that can eat you, and lets you know if you're able to take some time off in their gut
						Functions from the inventory as well as normal accessory slots
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Most things that can eat you [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:display their stomach capacity as predators above themselves].
						If their capacity number is [c/00FF00:green], they're able to swallow you with ease.
						[c/7F7F7F:This means that your choice predator could fit you in their stomach normally, and nothing is keeping them from gobbling you up on sight. Ready to get gurgled?]
						If their capacity number is [c/FFFF00:yellow], they're able to swallow you, but might have a bit of trouble keeping you down or properly mulching you.
						[c/7F7F7F:This means that while your target pred could fit you in their stomach normally, one of the following is true:]
						[c/7F7F7F:> Their stomach is too full to fit you due to other meals already inside it]
						[c/7F7F7F:> Your defense exceeds their digestion tick damage]
						[c/7F7F7F:> Your health exceeds 20 seconds of their stomach's final DDPS (digestion damage per second, factors in defense)]
						[c/7F7F7F:> Your acid resist level exceeds your desired predator's stomach's acid tier]
						If their capacity number is [c/FF0000:red], they aren't able to gulp and gurgle you into gut fat.
						[c/7F7F7F:This means that your target predator isn't able to eat you, since their stomach won't be able to hold you. A sad day, indeed.]
						Functions from the inventory as well as when equipped in normal accessory slots.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						Exposing an electronics implement to shimmer, most times, doesn't actually short-circuit it like water or stomach acid might, but instead tends to warp the implement's functionality to a new use case similar to, yet also very different, its initial purpose.
						This almost otherworldy-looking device performs a similar task to its non-shimmered counterpart, but analyzes the digestive capacity of scanned subjects instead. While this is useful for anyone looking to get mulched by a nice, hungry tummy, it's not particularly useful to a predator in comparison to its normal form.
						'''
				}
			}

			Vanity: {
				BalloonBelly: {
					Short:
						'''
						Can be blown up or deflated, and wrapped around your tummy to make it look bigger!
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Can be worn in any vanity accessory slot to make your stomach always appear larger proportional to the size of the balloon.
						Current size is {InflatedSize}; maximum size is {MaximumInflatedSize}.
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] to inflate the balloon if it is not at its max size, increasing its size by 1.
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Right-click] to deflate the balloon if it has air in it, decreasing its size by 1.
						Does nothing when equipped in a non-vanity accessory slot.
						'''
					Flavor: This funny-looking balloon is pre-fitted with a waistband for easy attachment to...well, specifically the stomach. Blow it up enough, and it'll replicate all the great looks of a massive, meat-filled gut without any of the downsides, complete with color-changing latex exterior so you get just the matching color you and your tummy want! Just note that it won't make all the happy gurgling and groaning a REAL bellyful of squirmy snacks makes.
				}
			}

			AntiDigestionSash: {
				Short:
					'''
					Decreases taken digestion damage and slows Softened buildup slightly
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases taken digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{AntiDigestionSashDigestionDefenseBonus}].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Slows Softened buildup] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{AntiDigestionSashSoftenedBuildupReduction}].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A simple sash made out of leathers, feathers, and silk, often hastily put together and worn by less confident adventurers.
					While it won't hold up to a continued gastric assault, it can help stave off the acids of a hungry tummy in a pinch.
					'''
			}

			HungryCursorEnabler: {
				Short:
					'''
					...what does this...do?
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Allows your cursor to eat certain entities] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:pressing Swallow Item while hovering over them with nothing in your hand].
					[c/7F7F7F:>] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:No swallow capacity limit (+ can swallow bosses)]
					[c/7F7F7F:> Stomach capacity:] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:{MiniCandyFairyStomachCapacity}]
					[c/7F7F7F:>] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Cannot be escaped]
					[c/7F7F7F:> Digestion tick damage:] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:{CursorDigestDamage}]
					[c/7F7F7F:> Digestion tick rate:] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:{CursorDigestRate}/sec]
					[c/7F7F7F:> Absorption rate:] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:{CursorAbsorbRate}/min]
					Your cursor [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:digests better] while you're sleeping.
					[c/7F7F7F:> 1.25x digestion tick rate and absorption rate; also makes both scale with the speed of time.]
					'''
				Flavor: An incredibly strange item which rests ominously in your hand. It takes the shape of a digital screen's cursor, yet trying to use it directly bears no fruit. Even if we don't assume this strange artifact is probably itself a mimic (or at the very least wants to eat you), given it came from inside one, just what purpose could it serve that requires this particular shape...?
			}

			NymphHairScarf: {
				Short:
					'''
					Increases movement speed and lowers stomach weight
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases movement speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{NymphScarfMoveSpeedBuff}].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{NymphScarfWeightReduction}].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A pleasantly comfortable scarf sewn with the luscious locks of at least one or two delicious, deceitful damsels found throughout Terraria's great caverns.
					Sewn into the scarf are sapphires and miniature runes which allow the wearer to be lighter on their feet, even (or perhaps, especially) with a good gutful of meat (still alive or otherwise) slowing them down, mimicking the stomach-centric swiftness of a hungry nymph.
					'''
			}

			PromethiaAntiDigestionSash: {
				Short:
					'''
					Decreases taken digestion damage and slows Softened buildup substantially
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases taken digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PromethiaAntiDigestionSashDigestionDefenseBonus}].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Slows Softened buildup] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PromethiaAntiDigestionSashSoftenedBuildupReduction}].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A sparkly, tasty-looking sash made of a material similar to gold, yet possessing the consistency of silk...as well as some actual divine-looking silk, this sash is standard-issue equipment for lower-ranking Sinhunters from the heavens beyond.
					It holds up against greedier gastric assaults much better than its mortally-designed counterpart, and is designed to grant eaten angels some time to properly teach their predator just how low said predator still is on the greater food chain.
					St. Promethia, of course, keeps hers with her not because she wants to get out of the predators that snack on her, but rather, because she wants just a little more time to...enjoy herself, for lack of a better term, inside those hungry tummies.
					'''
			}

			ShroomNecklace: {
				Short:
					'''
					Increases your max number of minions by 1
					Strengthens your fungal fairies
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Increases your maximum number of minions] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:1].
					Confers the following buffs to fungal fairies you own summoned by the [i:V2/ShroomStaff] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Fungal Fairy Staff]:
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Halved] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:movement speed penalty] from weight gain.
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:1.35x] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:food absorption rate].
					- Fungal spores grant [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:'Fungal Blessing'] for [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:4] seconds each [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:(or ][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:12 seconds][c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}: if eaten)].
					'''
				Flavor: A blue necklace, fitted with a mysterious mushroom that seems to leave a positive impact on fungal fairies.
			}
		}

		Charms: {
			BetterDigestion: {
				Short:
					'''
					Makes your acids a little bit stronger
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long: "[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases ACI] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{AcidStrengthBonus}]."
				Flavor: A beginner-level charm designed to make the bearer's stomach acids substantially more potent than if they were to go without it. Very useful for first-time predators who could really use that extra kick to their digestive juices to secure their first few big meals, though sadly not particularly worthwhile past those starting stages.
			}

			Fatass: {
				Short:
					'''
					Lets you take on much bigger prey...but at what cost?
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Doubles] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:swallow and stomach capacities].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Halves] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:digestion damage and tick rate].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A high-risk, high-reward charm typically only offered to skilled adventurers with a greedy enough tummy to negate its downside; it is often plucked from these adventurers by nymphs as one of the few things that can survive the gastric torment of such deceitful ladies' gluttonous tummies.
					While worn, it redirects a part of the muscle and nerve firings from actively digesting swallowed prey, instead putting that bodily power towards stretching the throat and stomach to gobble up and gorge oneself on ever-larger prey. It's not hard to see why nymphs see them as a valuable trinket, as would anyone else.
					'''
			}

			LessStomachWeight: {
				Short:
					'''
					Makes your stomach lighter, but only if you're not too full
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{WeightReduction}].
					If your stomach is at {FullnessEffectivenessLossThreshold} fullness or more, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:this effect becomes less effective the less capacity you have to spare.]
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A rather strange charm, almost mechanical in nature, purpose-built to make one's stomach significantly less of a burden to lug around while it's filled to capacity with sufficiently satisfying caloric fuel.
					While it works in most cases, it does this by passively generating a layer of helium inside of the bearer's stomach; thus, if there isn't sufficient room to provide said helium deposits, the charm becomes significantly less effective, to the point of eventually doing nothing if there is no space to add helium.
					'''
			}

			PreyItemTheft: {
				Short:
					'''
					May cause you to belch up certain items from your meals
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Upon dying to digestion,] prey you eat [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:have a chance to drop certain items].
					Some items dropped this way will be [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:unique] to these tables, while others will be [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:existing drops] from the prey (with [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:lower/limited drop rates]).
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A very simple charm.
					The only noteworthy thing about it is the big, shiny...tasty coin...perfectly...in the center...

					...donning it makes you feel incredibly...hungry. Hungry for valuables. Maybe your future meals would be kind enough to give you some so you don't end up snacking on your tasty new charm?
					'''
			}

			RegenFromAbsorption: {
				Short:
					'''
					Grants health and mana regeneration while digesting dead prey
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					While digesting dead prey, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:based on how much you absorb in a minute:]
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{HealthRegenerationRatio} of absorption rate in HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Natural)]
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ManaHeal}:Increases mana regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{ManaRegenerationRatio} of absorption rate in MP/sec].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:Effectiveness decreases if there are prey in your stomach still alive.]

					Current regeneration ({RegenEffectiveness} effectiveness with {LivePreyRemaining} out of {PreyRemaining} prey still alive):
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:{CurrentHealthRegen} HP/sec]
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.ManaHeal}:{CurrentManaRegen} mana/sec]
					'''
				Flavor: An intermediate-level charm designed to ease the long-standing issue of one's digestive system granting surprisingly little reprieve from the heat of battle. As long as a surplus of food resides in the bearer's stomach, this charm will convert some of the excess calories into mana to fuel a spell which revitalizes the bearer both physically and magically. Of course, this spell can only work as quickly as the bearer's belly can digest its meals.
			}
		}

		Consumables: {
			Catchables: {
				Pinky: {
					Short:
						'''
						When used, a delicious little Pinky is released into the world
						Hold the Swallow key while using this item to instantly gulp down the released Pinky
						Has a very pleasantly sweet taste, granting a few buffs when eaten
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						When eaten by anything:
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:Heals for {PinkyEatHeal} health] instantly upon running out of health.
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Grants the Happy! buff] while in a stomach; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{PinkyEatHappyLength} seconds] once fully digested.
						- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Grants the Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{PinkyEatRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
						May have any number of positive consequences if given to someone as a sweet treat of a gift.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						With how diverse slimes are in size, shape, and savor, it's no surprise that some slimes end up hunted almost exclusively for their beloved flavor. No slime embodies this more directly than the Pinky, a very small slime which is HIGHLY prized for the following traits:
						1) Its bite-size nature, allowing even the smallest and most inexperienced or incapable of predators to swallow it with relative ease.
						2) Its lovely flavor, which much resembles cotton candy, though almost all are uncertain as to where this sweet flavoring actually originated.
						3) Its vibrant pink coloration, from which it gets its name.
						'''
				}

				Butterflies: {
					Generic: {
						BaseWeight: This butterfly doesn't seem to have had any particularly good meals, judging from the unfortunate lack of fat on its frame.
						WeightGain1: This butterfly seems to be eating okay; a small deposit of chub has formed on its abdominals.
						WeightGain2: This butterfly seems to be eating decently; a healthy amount of flab has been stocked up around its belly.
						# for later
						WeightGain3: ""
						WeightGain4: ""
						WeightGain5: ""
						WeightGain6: ""
						WeightGain7: ""
						WeightGain8: ""
						WeightGain9: ""
						WeightGain10: Your finger sinks into the butterfly's plush expanses of fat as you poke it, and you can't help but wonder if you'll be next up in there...for better or worse.
					}

					Monarch: {
						Flavor: A species of butterfly named partially for its majestic coloration, and partially for the fact that one was the gastric tomb of Queen Andria Maria von Sember VII of Avarsici and three of her four royal daughters. The lone surviving daughter kept that butterfly as a pet, and kept it very well-fed with wannabe rival princesses until she took the throne.

						WeightGain1: {
							Short:
								'''
								When used, a harmless little butterfly is released into the world
								Hold the Swallow key while using this item to instantly gulp down the released butterfly
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
								'''
							Long: Has no special effects when eaten.
							Flavor:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Consumables.Catchables.Butterflies.Monarch.Flavor}
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Consumables.Catchables.Butterflies.Generic.WeightGain1}
								'''
						}

						WeightGain2: {
							Short:
								'''
								When used, a harmless little butterfly is released into the world
								Hold the Swallow key while using this item to instantly gulp down the released butterfly
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
								'''
							Long: Has no special effects when eaten.
							Flavor:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Consumables.Catchables.Butterflies.Monarch.Flavor}
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Consumables.Catchables.Butterflies.Generic.WeightGain2}
								'''
						}
					}

					PurpleEmperor: {
						Flavor: Named for being the favorite butterfly of King Markus Caldera, who many referred to as the 'Elegant Purple Emperor' of a golden-age Avarsici, this butterfly eats like royalty: dining upon only the fanciest of flowers, living or otherwise. If offered, it will also help itself to any maids or butlers in the area.

						WeightGain1: {
							Short:
								'''
								When used, a harmless little butterfly is released into the world
								Hold the Swallow key while using this item to instantly gulp down the released butterfly
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
								'''
							Long: Has no special effects when eaten.
							Flavor:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Consumables.Catchables.Butterflies.PurpleEmperor.Flavor}
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Consumables.Catchables.Butterflies.Generic.WeightGain1}
								'''
						}

						WeightGain2: {
							Short:
								'''
								When used, a harmless little butterfly is released into the world
								Hold the Swallow key while using this item to instantly gulp down the released butterfly
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
								'''
							Long: Has no special effects when eaten.
							Flavor:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Consumables.Catchables.Butterflies.PurpleEmperor.Flavor}
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Consumables.Catchables.Butterflies.Generic.WeightGain2}
								'''
						}
					}

					RedAdmiral: {
						Flavor: This butterfly, surprisingly, is ACTUALLY named for its coloration, being resemblant of a sea dog's finest red-and-black garb when its wings are fully spread. Perhaps rather fittingly, it prefers to eat seafood, be it plant or fish.

						WeightGain1: {
							Short:
								'''
