			PermanentUpgrades: {
				PureSwallowBoost1: {
					Short:
						'''
						Permanently increases the strength of your throat when used or eaten
						Can only be used once; further uses and/or consumptions do nothing special
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Using or eating this item] will permanently grant you the following bonus:
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases GLP] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{PureSwallow1GLPBonus}].
						This bonus only applies once. Using or eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:will have no further effect].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						One of the first physical stimulants for predators ever created was a drug to enhance the potential of the throat, allowing for easier swallowing of anything, and anyone, that the recipient wanted packed into their gut.
						This stimulant has been replicated countless times, and is now standard-fare as an entry-level predatory aid across the world of Terraria.
						'''
				}
			}

			Potions: {
				FastDigestionPotion: {
					Short:
						'''
						Speeds up digestion while digesting
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Induces a variety of predatorily-centric effects when drank, almost all involving digestive power.
						Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
						You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

						Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 1 minute thereafter:
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:+{FastDigestionPotionACIBonus} ACI]
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:+{FastDigestionPotionABSBonus} ABS]
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Raises acid tier to 3][c/7F7F7F:, if it is not at 3 already]
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						Digestive aids are commonplace in medical establishments across Terraria to help with particularly rowdy or troublesome prey, with just about every option that entails available for use to make sure your system doesn't get backed up with all the parts of your prey you can't quite melt down (yet).
						This is a rather simple variant carried by medical practitioners at all times (be they for your use or theirs). Dropping something small into the bottle seems to cause it to be swiftly dissolved by the mysterious substance within...not that it's much of a surprise, really. Even inanimate objects can be ravenously hungry --- enough to eat a person, in the right circumstance. People just always seem to make great meals...

						...well, that snack in your stomach won't wait much longer. Bon appetit!
						'''
				}

				StomachCapacityPotion: {
					Short:
						'''
						Allows your stomach to hold a bit more than usual while digesting
						'For when you're craving an extra snack or two for dessert'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Improves your stomach's holding capacity when drank.
						Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
						You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

						Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter:
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:+{StomachCapacityPotionCapacityBonus} stomach capacity]
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						A commonplace and easily-brewable predatory enhancer in the Terrarian world, this potion uses a simple mix of relaxing agents, mainly found in fish, to allow a predator's stomach to stretch a good bit past its normal limits.
						Sadly, though, it won't bolster your stomach's durability against internal fighting at all; you'd best hope you can keep down all that extra meat you'll be able to fit into your hungry tummy.
						'''
				}

				StomachacheMeterCapacityPotion: {
					Short:
						'''
						Improves your stomach's resistance to the struggles of your prey while digesting
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Improves your stomach's ability to keep prey from causing a ruckus inside you when drank.
						Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
						You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

						Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter:
						> [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Increases stomachache meter capacity] by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{StomachacheMeterCapacityPotionMeterCapacityBonus}].
						> The struggles of your prey will deal [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:-{StomachacheMeterCapacityPotionUneaseDefenseBonus} less struggle damage].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						One of a number of common brews made for predatory types, this potion is often sold by medical practitioners to those who need that one particularly feisty femme or burly breakfast they had to settle down and digest, ideally without hacking them back up.
						It makes use of several well-known gastric relaxants to ease the stomach and throat, lowering the amount that unruly prey can kick up a stomachache and heightening the amount they'd need to do so in order to induce vomiting.
						'''
				}
			}

			SpecialItemUpgrades: {
				PaperMaidSummon: {
					RawStats: {
						Short:
							'''
							{PaperMaidName} might like this item
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							This item can be fed to {PaperMaidName}, the paper maid summoned by the [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{$Mods.V2.ItemName.Voraria.Weapons.Summon.PaperMaidSummon}], by right-clicking on her with it.
							Once she fully digests this item, {PaperMaidName} will permanently gain automagic self-lamination, conferring to her the following buffs:
							> +{LaminatedHealth} health.
							> +{LaminatedStomachCapacity} stomach capacity.
							> +{LaminatedStomachacheMeterCapacity} stomachache meter capacity.
							> +{LaminatedDigestionRatio} digestion damage ratio.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							This small device, a marvel of magical conduction cross-bred with machine lamination, is designed to be able to laminate anything and everything simply by placing the desired item inside it and waiting.
							Early prototypes proved incapable of accepting people as input and laminating. These prototypes have since been stored in their creator's personal stash for later dismantling.
							That said, while lamination is often used as a tool to hunt origami creations in the wild, fallen off trading caravans and originally left over from Sveetia's annual Sugar Crane Festival, it is also used by the Sveetian people to reinforce their greatest works.
							'''
					}

					Flight: {
						Short:
							'''
							{PaperMaidName} might like this item
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							This item can be fed to {PaperMaidName}, the paper maid summoned by the [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{$Mods.V2.ItemName.Voraria.Weapons.Summon.PaperMaidSummon}], by right-clicking on her with it.
							Once she fully digests this item, {PaperMaidName} will permanently gain paper crane wings, conferring the following buffs:
							> Gains flight capabilities, and will fly as her master or target does.
							> Increased accuracy and range for dash attack ([c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:RIGHT-RIGHT-RIGHT] instruction).
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A poor, damaged origami crane, worn down by evading the ever-growing hunger of the average office worker for a nice, well-laminated snack from Sveetia while on lunch break.
							While its wings are battered and its flight rendered all but gone, it still has strength to give...but not to those who would hunt it for a light meal.
							No, this weak, dying crane searches for another of its kin, another Sveetian origami piece, to give itself wholly to...

							...lending, to that creation, the great power of flight.
							'''
					}
				}
			}

			DigestionRepairScroll: {
				Short:
					'''
					Using this item will instantly relieve you of most of the downsides of predator or preything lifestyles
					After it is used, a full day must pass before it can be used again
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					This item can only be used once at least one full day has passed since the last time it was used.
					Upon usage, it will instantly:
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Fully repair all items in your inventory] that have taken digestion damage and can be repaired.
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Remove all Softened stacks still applied to you] from any lingering acid burns from recent encounters.
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Clear all indigestion-related debuffs you may have] from particularly troublesome meals.
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					It's a scroll, inscribed with countless runes that you've never seen before; notably, they look surprisingly similar to, yet so very different from, musical notes...which would help, if the scroll bothered to say anything about the actual composition of the piece. Whoever wrote this sheet music didn't think it through very well from the perspective of one who might want to play it.
					In any event, incomprehensible as it may be at a cursory glance, as you go to look at it closer, the runes fade into the background somewhat, and a second layer of text fades in which is actually comprehensible to the average person:

					[c/FF3FBF:CHORUS (sing in D# major):]
					[c/FF3FBF:From heavens inward and a cauldron outward, the Songstress' graces shall smile.]
					[c/FF3FBF:By Melodia's song, this verse, if not wrong, shall save from a fate all too vile.]

					[c/FF3FBF:I near face the Veil, the edge of our great hail, as a chance predator's left me weak,]
					[c/FF3FBF:So by Melodia's song, I sing a chorus along, for my strength to return to its peak.]

					[c/7F1F5F:POST-CHORUS (composer's note):]
					[c/7F1F5F:But the song must rest, asleep in its nest, 'fore its strength can remend its own peak,]
					[c/7F1F5F:So by my sacred song, don't dare sing this wrong; I care not for the melodically weak.]
					'''
			}

			DigestionUpgradeTablets: {
				Short:
					'''
					Can only be eaten once you've fully gained the stomach-strengthening effects of Life Fruit and enchanted your stomach acids beforehand
					Permanently modifies your digestive system using a delayed-effect bioalteration spell once fully digested
					This mixes nitric acid into the structure of your stomach acid, turning it into aqua regia (royal water)
					This change makes your stomach significantly better at digesting things, and allows you to digest more things you wouldn't normally be able to
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					This item can only be eaten once you have eaten and digested at least {LifeCrystalsMax} Life Crystals, at least {ManaCrystalsMax} Mana Crystals, and at least {LifeFruitMax} Life Fruits.
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently grants +40 ACI.]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Permanently grants +20 ABS.]
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:Raises your acid tier to Royal (2).]
					This upgrade is permanent, but only takes effect once the pack is fully digested.
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					Despite how often these things were flaunted around as the future of predatory prowess and a marvel of modern magical bioengineering back in the day, the real marvel is that these somehow pose no significant health risks despite mixing an entire secondary acid into an already-powerful stomach. The label on the side suggests eating the entire pack...including the pack itself. The pack supposedly has much better nutritional value than the pills, so...bottoms up.
					Obtaining more than one pack of these tablets is prohibited by Avarsician law and punishable by...well, predominantly fucking about and learning what for. It's not exactly hard to guess why a spell that assumes you haven't taken the pills at all is bad if you've already melted down a full pack of them before.
					'''
			}

			FeatherDuster: {
				Short:
					'''
					Can only be used in a hungry tummy
					Can be used to tickle and/or agitate your predator's stomach a lot; often enough for them to belch you back up
					'Now taken very literally'
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					Can only be used while inside something's stomach.
					When used, instantly [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:deals] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{FeatherDusterStruggleDamage}] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:struggle damage] to your predator.
					If this would fill up their stomachache meter, it instead caps at its usual maximum, and you are [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:instantly belched out].
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					Often carried around by the bundle by harpies, the core purpose of this feathery broom-like implement is to agitate the stomach of hungry predators, forcing them to belch and/or cough up whatever (and WHOever) they ate alongside the user.
					More modern uses for evolved forms of this implement include maids' cleaning work, on-the-job snacks for said maids, impromptu microphones-turned-mini-meals on budget karaoke nights, and mitigating a wide array of magical incantations.
					'''
			}

			HairDyeCapacity: {
				Short:
					'''
					Changes the color of your hair based on how full you are
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Changes the color of your hair] based on [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:how full your stomach currently is].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:When your stomach is empty], makes your hair a dark red.
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:When your stomach is completely full], makes your hair a pleasantly full green.
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A special hair dye, purpose-mixed for the fashionable predator in your life (be it yourself or someone else).
					On a full stomach, this dye gives off a stunningly pleasant green, while the dark red one's hair will turn while running on empty is just as attractive. A number of other colors end up in the spotlight if the wearer's stomach isn't 100% full, but still has some meat in it, and all of them are specially designed to make one's hair as appealing as possible.
					After all, how can your prey resist ending up a part of those luscious locks if you've got just the right color to make them weak in the knees?

					DISCLAIMER: Excess calories from digested meals may not actually increase hair length.
					'''
			}

			SteampunkerGutFastTravel: {
				Short:
					'''
					Can only be used in a hungry tummy?
					Can be used to save yourself from impending digestion into ass fat, probably?
					'The latest and greatest in instantaneous transportation!...or so she says.'
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					Can only be used while the Steampunker is alive.
					When used, instantly [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:teleports you] [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:out of your current predator's stomach], if applicable...[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:and into the Steampunker's].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:Does not work] while in the Steampunker's stomach.
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					A peculiar little trinket fashioned together by the Steampunker, the great lass she is, for a measly sum.
					It can be used anywhere as a one-way teleport, even workable in the most gluttonous guts to instantly get you out of digestive jeopardy...but to what catch?
					Much to the Steampunker's frustration, though, it doesn't yet work across planes of reality, nor from excessively long distances. She's still working on that functionality.
					'''
			}

			DemonCandy: {
				Short:
					'''
					Provides regeneration when digested
					'Isn't this just a jawbreaker covered in chocolate?'
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					When eaten:
					- [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Grants the Regeneration buff] after running out of durability; this lingers for [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:{Regen} minutes].
					If dropped onto the ground in the Underworld, it might bait out certain types of monsters.
					'''
				Flavor:
					'''
					It is, infact, a jawbreaker covered in chocolate.
					Appears to be the favourite food of a certain type of monster in the lava-filled depths of the Underworld.
					'''
			}

			GhostBall: {
				Short:
					'''
					If a certain ghost isn't present, throwing this into a surface will summon them
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long: "[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Summons Echo], who behaves similar to a Town Pet. You will be able to have them live in a house with another Town NPC."
				Flavor: Not quite a spirit bomb, but you can pretend it is, i guess.
			}
		}

		Tools: {
			PredToggleRod: {
				Short:
					'''
					Can be used to fine-tune inanimate objects' appetites
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
			}
		}

		TransformationItems: {
			BaelzTransformationItem: {
				Short:
					'''
					Transforms you into a chaotic rat girl while in the inventory
					You may be susceptible to weight gain under the effect
					Right click to toggle effect
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					While active:
					By default, you have [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:+10%] critical chance, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:+15%] attack speed,
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:+30%] movement speed, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:-35%] damage, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:-15%] damage reduction,
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:-20%] stomach capacity & [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:+25%] absorption rate
					Critical chance increases when gaining weight.
					On a critical hit, the chance is rolled again, dealing a double crit that [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:doubles damage] if successful.
					Additionally, prey in your stomach can take critical damage, using the critical chance given by this item.
					'''
				Flavor: tba
			}

			KroniiTransformationItem: {
				Short:
					'''
					Transforms you into a (seemingly) elegant lady while in the inventory
					You may be susceptible to weight gain under the effect
					Right click to toggle effect
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					While active:
					By default, you have +10% movement speed, +20% jump height, -25% damage reduction,
					+33% body weight reduction, -1 flat body weight & -15% stomach weight reduction.
					Melee attacks add 1.25 seconds of [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:Time Acceleration], which increases melee attack speed, acid & absorption effectiveness.
					Time Acceleration can stack up to [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:30 seconds].
					Melee attacks additionally have a [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:10% chance to freeze an enemy in time] for [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:2 seconds].
					This chance is affected by luck.
					After the enemy is unfrozen, they cannot be frozen again for a second, or 5 seconds if it's a boss.
					'''
				Flavor: tba
			}

			OllieTransformationItem: {
				Short:
					'''
					Transforms you into a crazy zombie girl while in the inventory
					You may be susceptible to weight gain under the effect
					Right click to toggle effect
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					While active:
					By default, you have [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:+20%] movement speed, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:+45%] stomach capacity, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:-1] flat stomach weight,
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:+67%] stomach weight reduction, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:-67%] acid damage, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:-67%] absorption rate & [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThing}:-10%] ranged damage.
					Non-homing ranged attacks deal more damage the further away the target is, up to [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:1.75x damage].
					You can [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:dash toward your cursor] by pressing [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:(Ollie: Dash)], dodging enemies and projectiles while granting
					a [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThing}:drastically increased firing rate] for a short time.
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:You may also end up 'accidentally' swallowing things you dash into...]
					'''
				Flavor: tba
			}

			SoraTransformationItem: {
				Short:
					'''
					Transforms you into an idol while in the inventory
					You may be susceptible to weight gain under the effect
					Right click to toggle effect
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long: tba
				Flavor: tba
			}

			MintTransformationItem: {
				Short:
					'''
					Transforms you into a ghost maid while in the inventory
					You may be susceptible to weight gain under the effect
					Right click to toggle effect
					{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
					'''
				Long:
					'''
					While active:
					Ghost and ghostlike enemies are instantly absorbed into your stomach on contact.
					A wisp meter appears below you, filling up as you absorb prey.
					The size of the meter and the rate it fills up is based on your maximum amount of minion slots.
					Once a segment of the meter has filled, you can press (Mint: Summon Wisp) to summon a friendly wisp minion.
					The wisp fires projectiles at nearby enemies, and after 7 shots, may charge into an enemy to explode.
					'''
				Flavor: tba
			}
		}

		Weapons: {
			Ranged: {
				Throwables: {
					FragileBottles: {
						Generic: {
							Short:
								'''
								Can be thrown to coat a target in {ThrowableBottleLowercaseCondimentName}
								Coated targets may attract the appetites of certain predators
								Will damage friendly entities
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] to throw a bottle of {ThrowableBottleLowercaseCondimentName}.
								The bottle [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:deals 100% damage] to the first entity it hits, shattering instantly.
								Struck enemies are [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:coated in {ThrowableBottleLowercaseCondimentName}] for 20 seconds.
								'''
							Flavor: For virtually as long as humanoids have existed on Terraria, they have tried to find numerous ways to coat their prey, living and otherwise, in delicious substances to enhance their flavor. A popular pick amongst modern-day brawlers is these throwable bottles, shattering on impact and coating prey in whatever they contain.
						}

						Honey: {
							Short: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Short}"
							Long:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Long}
								Honey-coated snacks will attract the attention of predators that like [c/FF7FBF:sweet] flavors.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Flavor}
								This bottle contains a healthy helping of sweet, delicious honey, sourced from the genuinely obscenely large bee hives scattered about Terrarian jungles. A single sip enlightens the tongue with a sugary-sweet flavor that, while by far beaten out by Sveetian sugar and its resultant papercrafts, still brings happiness to the mind. Any predator with a sweet tooth is sure to come a-hunting prey coated in this stuff.
								'''
						}

						HotSauce: {
							Short: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Short}"
							Long:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Long}
								Hot sauce-coated snacks will attract the attention of predators that like [c/FF7F00:spicy] flavors.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Flavor}
								This bottle contains a healthy helping of dangerously-hot Luke's Lightweight Lava(tm), a brand of hot sauce based in Desperais which Lucinda and countless other demons buy in bulk on the regular. A single sip trials the tongue with a scorching-hot sensation akin to drinking lava straight out of the lake...just without any of the gastrointestinal death that comes with unprotected lava drinking. Any predator craving some spice in their diet is bound to come running for prey coated in this stuff.
								'''
						}
					}
				}
			}

			Summon: {
				PaperMaidSummon: {
					Short:
						'''
						Summons a capable maid(...?) to fight for you
						She requires {NeededMinionSlots} minion slots available to be summoned, and has no sisters
						Can throw paper plates and simple silverware at enemies, as well as eat them or you
						Prey she eats get papercuts as they digest
						If eaten, she gives internal papercuts to her predator (intentionally or not) until sufficiently digested
						'Maidche to serve'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] to summon a maid to your cursor position. Her name is {Name}!
						{Name} requires {NeededMinionSlots} minion slots available to be summoned. There can only be one of her at once.
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] again while summoned and no instructions are being performed to teleport {Name} to your position.
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Right-click] to select the closest entity to the cursor for targeting. From here, you can command {Name} by inputting specific click combinations:
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:RIGHT-LEFT-LEFT] to have {Name} throw a paper plate at the target, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:dealing {PaperPlateDamage} damage].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:RIGHT-LEFT-RIGHT] to have {Name} throw a set of paper mache silverware at the target, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:dealing 3x{SilverwarePerDamage} damage].
						> The fork [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:ignores up to {ForkArmorPen} defense].
						> The spoon [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:deals {SpoonInorganicDamageBonusPercent} higher damage to inorganics].
						> The knife [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:inflicts Bleeding on applicable enemies for {KnifeBleedTime} seconds].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:RIGHT-RIGHT-LEFT] to have {Name} swing a broom at the target if close enough, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:dealing {BroomDamage} damage].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:RIGHT-RIGHT-RIGHT] to have {Name} dash towards the target. If she contacts the target in this state, she immediately snatches them into her mouth, swallowing them in short order.
						{Name}'s stomach has a [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:capacity of {StomachCapacity}] and a [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:stomachache meter capacity of {StomachacheMeterCapacity}].
						{Name}'s stomach [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:deals {DigestionDamage} digestion damage {DigestionRate} times per second].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:{DigestionBleedRatio} of digestion damage] is instead [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:converted to a Bleeding proc which persists even if prey escape] her stomach.
						If eaten by anything, {Name} has {Health} health, and [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Damage}:passively inflicts Bleeding on her predator] until she dies from digestion.
						If eaten by you, {Name} [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:will not struggle in your stomach].
						If you feed yourself to {Name}, her stomach will not digest you unless you ask to be digested.
						While in {Name}'s stomach:
						> She will not eat any other prey, even if they try to weasel their way into her mouth, unless you are already being digested.
						> The [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:RIGHT-RIGHT-RIGHT] input can be performed inside {Name}'s stomach to [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:instruct her to digest you].
						> All damage dealt to her is redirected to her stomachache meter.
						> If her stomachache meter fills, you and any other contained still-alive prey will be forcefully ejected.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						A well-crafted origami piece; one of countless made by the master papersmiths that populate the country of Sveetia, known for its acres upon acres of highly-prized sugar cane.
						This bell, when rung, cuts off and unfolds an infinitesmally small piece of itself, soon refashioning and refolding that mere speck into a sizable maid, ready to serve any master that needs her.
						Able to subdue foes in a wide variety of fashions, her preferred method is, of course, swallowing her targets whole so as to minimize and efficiently remove external clutter, living or otherwise.
						'''
				}

				ShroomFairySummon: {
					Short:
						'''
						Summons fungal fairies to protect you from long-range attacks by swallowing them up
						'A bunch of fun gals, really'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:Left-click] to summon a fungal fairy to your cursor position.
						Each fungal fairy requires 1.5 minion slots available to be summoned.
						While active, fungal fairies will [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:dash over to and devour hostile projectiles] that stray too close to you.
						If they become too full of tasty enemy ranged attacks, they'll have to take a moment to rest and digest before they can actively gobble up more.
						As they gain weight, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:they'll digest faster and be able to hold more in their tums], [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:at the cost of moving slightly slower].
						While digesting, fungal fairies [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:release healing spores] that [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Heal}:heal for 5 health upon contact, or 10 if you swallow them].
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						Magical implements used by adventurers that have since lost their lives to the gluttony of the undergrowth are often twisted by wherever they happen to get got. This poor thing's owner must have perished in a cave full of mushrooms.
						Notably, the fairies that stay around these preferred regions seemed to like implements like these a lot; if you were to shake this about, perhaps one would come to your aid and shield you from oncoming fire (with, of course, their greedy tummy).
						'''
				}
			}

			Throwing: {
				Knives: {
					PiranhaTooth: {
						Short:
							'''
							Inflicts Bleeding on struck enemies
							Deals bonus damage to organic enemies
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
							'''
						Long: TO BE ADDED TO AEM
						Flavor: TO BE ADDED TO AEM
					}
				}
			}
		}

		FlyingFishScale: {
			Short:
				'''
				Not very useful, but may sell well
				{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
				'''
			Long:
				'''
				Can be obtained by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:killing or digesting a Flying Fish].
				Sells well to merchants.
				'''
			Flavor: A small scale cut from a flying fish, no doubt alongside a batch of others. While they aren't particularly useful thanks to the rain flying fish swim in making them slicker than usual, they taste nice and sell quite well.
		}

		NymphHairStrand: {
			Short:
				'''
				Used to make Sky Blue Dye
				{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
				'''
			Long:
				'''
				Can be obtained by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:digesting a Nymph].
				Can be used to make Sky Blue Dye at a Dye Vat.
				'''
			Flavor: A lock of a nymph's succulent silvery-blue hair, somehow spared from the gastric gauntlet of a gut such as yours. One could make a potent dye or a comfortable scarf out of this. A hair stylist would also quite like something as unique as this...
		}

		ObserverPupil: {
			Short:
				'''
				'Now I've seen everything.'
				{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
				'''
			Long: Can be obtained by [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:killing or digesting an Observer].
			Flavor: A large pupil from a huge yet harmless demon eye.
		}

		AstralFairyController: {
			Short:
				'''
				Allows you to command your Astral Fairy to consume anything you click on
				{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
				'''
			Long:
				'''
				You must have the Astral Fairy pet active for this item to function.
				Clicking on an NPC, projectile or dropped item teleports it straight into your fairy's gut.
				'''
			Flavor:
				'''
				Hold on, this isn't what you crafted...
				The Astral Fairy appears to react to it, in some way.
				'''
		}

		AstralFairySummon: {
			Short:
				'''
				Summons a fairy from the edge of the universe
				{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
				'''
			Long:
				'''
				Summons the Astral Fairy to hover above you
				On her own, she doesn't do much other than observe, however creating this item may create something else, too.
				'''
			Flavor:
				'''
				Her origins are unknown.
				She appears to bear a striking resemblance to the fungal fairies of this world, yet, unlike them, couldn't give two shits about eating, despite being very much capable of doing so.
				'''
		}

		DinnerBlaster: {
			Short:
				'''
				Shoots burgers that conveniently slip down predators' throats
				'I wonder what's for dinner'
				{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
				'''
			Long:
				'''
				Shoots floating burgers that get automatically eaten by predators on contact.
				The burgers have a size of [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.Action}:0.3].
				'''
			Flavor:
				'''
				My boy!
				I'm not gonna fight you, I'm gonna kick your ass!
				(Screaming)
				Spaghetti!
				NO-
				(Explosion)
				'''
		}

		MushroomToken: {
			Short:
				'''
				Can be used to craft certain items
				{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CheckTheAEM}
				'''
			Long:
				'''
				Dropped from fungal fairies once they reach a high enough weight
				Can be used to craft equipment related to them
				'''
			Flavor: A gift from one of your fungal fairies.
		}
	}
}

