		HairWindowGutCut: Gut Cut ({Price})
		HairWindowGutCutFree: Gut Cut (Free)
	}
}

TownNPCMood: {
	Angel: {
		Content: I- I'm doing wonderfully, thank you! Of course, if you'd like me to, I wouldn't object to...e- examining your internals...j- just in case there's any tonal dissonance in there! You'd be surprised how easy it can well up in even the b- best predators.
		NoHome: As...e- exciting as it is to study and experience the various i- ins and outs of the creatures of this world...w- well, I wouldn't mind someplace to stay as another home-away-from-home in my downtime between band practice and...w- well, my actual line of work.
		FarFromHome: W- wow! I've certainly traveled farther than usual today...hrm. What predatory thing could I have been attempting to s- soothe or s- study this far out...?

		Biomes: {
			Jungle: I absolutely LOVE this locale! Sure, it's awfully hot and humid here...oh, but just LOOK at all those hungry predators!~ I'm sure there's some glaring dissonance to be resolved with them! Sweet, sizzling, SCALDING dissonance...~
			Sky: It's always nice to be up in the skies...it reminds me a lot of home, in some ways. I do wonder how Melodia would like a place like this...m- maybe she'd be inspired to write a new song, even!
			Forest: I'm not sure I like it here. S- sure, it's very calm here, and the locals are nice, but...nothing here serves purpose for my job, and they're not very...e- enticing for me, either.
			Corruption: As fascinating as the specimens here are, this place is hardly suited for sustained housing! S- still...one must study the fallen to- well, to avoid BECOMING the fallen themselves...a- and the creatures here certainly get the mind m- moving...
			Crimson: This place is very...gorey. That said, the local...wildlife, if you can call them that, are certainly eager to...g- get me on my way into them...wh- which I don't mind all that m- much! Just...I can think of b- better places to do my work than here...
			Dungeon: I DESPISE this place. There's nothing worth studying. There's nothing to even EAT ME in the first place aside from the slimes. The slimes here are pointless to study, as ANY and all information about them could be gleaned from other, more visually-pleasing and scientifically-stimulating slimes. All of the humanoids I could be eaten by are specimens I could study literally ANYWHERE else. I'd very much like to leave.
		}

		Neighbors: {
			CrowdLevel: {
				Alone: It's very quiet here. I suppose the solitude isn't AWFUL, but...would you be so kind as to d- deliver the occasional pred with tum troubles to sweep me off of my feet a- and onto their figure?...f- for purely professional p- purposes, of course!
				GoodCompany: I enjoy the company you've given me. Very amicable, and very willing to further my work!...a- and generally give me a comfortable s- sytem to sit in and...s- soothe.
				BadCompany: I don't really enjoy the company you've given me. As for why...well, it varies from person to person.
				ThreesTheSweetSpot: Three is a c- crowd, they say...I- I say three is a healthy s- selection of potential p- predators to work with and analyze!...a- and throw myself into. I- it's not MY fault they need routine e- examinations!
				ThreesNotTheSweetSpot: Three is a crowd, they say. I- I say three WOULD be a healthy selection of potential predators to work with...i- if none of the elements were problematic.
				TooCrowded: I- is it a valid complaint in the field of m- medicinal gastronomy to be suffering from ch- choice paralysis!?
			}

			SpecificNPCs: {
				LoveSuccubus: Th- the demon lady? Lucinda!? I- I do NOT have...I d- don't...oh, who am I kidding? I- I could NEVER be anything less than s- SMITTEN for that b- beautiful body...and that s- strong, searing s- stomach...so STIMULATING! I o- only wish I had a professional reason t- to rest on her th- thighs for a while...
				LoveTavernkeep: "{NPCName}...the tavernk- keeper. Ooohhhhh...j- just LOOK at those arms. Those m- massive, manly muscles...unf, my t- temperature's rising just THINKING about him! I- I can only imagine how s- strong and s- sturdy his s- s- stomach must be...d- do you think he needs a medicinal g- gastronomer to snack on...?~"
				LikeNurse: "{NPCName} is such a wonderful woman, m- making sure everyone is happy, healthy, AND healthily hungry!...p- primarily because they can't really help me with my w- work if they're too sick to e- eat me."
				LikeDryad: Dryads are a very fascinating creature from external AND i- internal perspectives, so it should be no surprise that I find {NPCName} particularly fruitful to study!...a- and particularly...a- attractive. N- not NEARLY as attractive as Melodia, mind you, but still attractive!
				DislikeZoologist: B- by all accounts, I should like {NPCName} more than I do. Her s- system...changes dramatically in certain conditions, providing a rare opportunity to s- study and potentially soothe two states at once...and yet, it just bothers me. M- maybe it's just because other people's i- internals are the same experience each time...her s- stomach is inconsistent by comparison.
				DislikeArmsDealer: "{NPCName} bothers me slightly. I- it's not even that he doesn't want to eat me, o- or that I don't let him; he's m- MORE than enthusiastic enough, a- and I don't mind helping him! The problem is, he's...n- not my type, but he keeps insisting he is."
				HateAngler: "{NPCName}? Oh, that little fisherman's no fun. Too young to eat me, too young to get WHY I want to be eaten so much on any front --- heavens, he doesn't even know who my employer IS --- and he poses no noticeably distinct qualities whatsoever except for how much of a little BRAT he is!"

				Calamity: {
					LikeAmidias: Th- that seahorse king is great! He always gives me all sorts of information about the- ...the marine life that once populated his old home! He, himself, is also quite...i- interesting...compared to most I meet!
					HateCalamitas: I once asked the witch to allow me to...s- study her internals for my job...a- and she threatened to burn me on the spot for asking! Seriously, what did HER boss m- make her put up with to make her such a k- killjoy!?
				}
			}
		}
	}

	Succubus: {
		Content: Aside from you not fillin' out my gut right now, I think I'm fine.
		NoHome: My stomach's a good spot for a good morsel like you, but I need a real place to live if I'm gonna feed this gut of mine on the regular.
		FarFromHome: Well, I've headed off a little far from home today, eh? Then again, it's all worth gettin' the right meal.

		Biomes: {
			Ocean: It's great to be around the ocean, don'tcha think? Sittin' in the warm sand, lookin' over the sunset as your prey-stuffed gut churns and gurgles even the meatiest meals into more of ya...it's the BEST. My only regret's that I didn't come up here sooner.
			Desert: The desert's nice and warm, I have to say. Reminds me of home, in all the good ways, and it's a lot more open to boot. Plenty of good prey to snatch up, too, if you know where to look. I like it.
			Tundra: It's way too cold around here, if you ask me. Food's a bit too fluffy for me, too. I'd kill for a warm lava bath right now; find me one, or at least a warmer place to crash.
			Corruption: Seriously!? This place is awful! I can't even eat the stuff here; I might get food poisoning from how rotten it all is!
			Crimson: I think you've officially put my appetite in a coma. Congratulations. I've never looked at a place like this before, and I'd never like to again.
			Underworld: Home again...honestly, I'm already sick enough of bein' here. Either help me cram at LEAST half of that city into my gut, buildings included, or help me move outta here...again.
			Dungeon: Look at this place...dark, moody, and not a single guy or gal to snack on in sight. It reminds me of home, in all the worst ways possible.
		}

		Neighbors: {
			CrowdLevel: {
				Alone: This area is pretty quiet, huh? Nobody to eat around here...but I guess the solitude ain't all that bad. Just be sure to gimme a sexy snack or seven every once in a while, alright?
				GoodCompany: This area's pretty quiet...but there's still a couple decent snacks around.
				BadCompany: This area's pretty quiet. Don't really like that, and I don't like the people you've got me with, either.
				GoodCrowd: I'm lovin' it here...plenty of healthy, meaty meals around to gulp down and get nice and fat off of. You're the best, y'know that?
				NeutralCrowd: It's a bit crowded here. Some good eats, sure, but you could probably stand to...burn off the fat, if you catch my drift.
				BadCrowd: Seriously!? You REALLY had to cram me in with all the WORST of this lot!?
			}

			SpecificNPCs: {
				LoveAngel: Promethia? That cute little angel that loves every chance she can get to cram herself into me? Hah...more like ProMEALthia, if you ask me.
				LoveZoologist: That busty bimbo of a fox'll look GREAT hangin' off my chest. Mind bringing her over here?~
				LikeNurse: You know, I think my gut needs a check-up from {NPCName}; it's just DYING to...get to know her a bit better. Think you can get her to find the time to stay on my waist for a while?~
				LikeGuide: I can't figure out why, but something about the idea of melting {NPCName} down into fat gets me all giddy for some reason.
				DislikeStylist: That hair stylist, Amber...she's a pretty spicy gal, isn't she? 'Course, that's nothing bad...I like spicy food. What I DON'T like is if that spice means they're not food. She's definitely spicy enough to try and eat me first. Not dumb enough to challenge that.
				HateAngler: If it weren't for the fact that children are way too small to be decent meals, that scrawny little fisherman brat would be padding out my waistline right now. Keep your TRASH off my lawn, got it?
				HateDryad: I'm really close to just using my stomach to solve the problem of {NPCName}'s constant preachin' about "purity" and "cleansing". Pompous bitch can't make an ass of herself about my eatin' habits if she's too busy fattenin' up mine, now, can she?
				HateTaxCollector: You've already done the impossible twice; once to get me outta that shithole I called home, and once to take down that massive fleshbag from the other edge. Do it a third time and get {NPCName} to either shut the hell up or move out; I'm already more than sick of him.

				Calamity: {
					DislikeCalamitas: There's bein' an apex predator, and then there's bein a stupid predator. Anyone tryin' to eat that grumpy old witch'll learn pretty fast that they're the latter...and I don't like that. Might scare off my food.
					HateAmidias: That old seahorse is just no fun at all. Won't let me have any, either. I honestly don't even feel like eating him. He's just...he's THAT kinda guy, y'know? Anyway, move him.
				}
			}
		}
	}

	Painter: {
		Content: Huh? Oh, am I good? Yeah, I'm fine right now. This is a good spot to paint.
		Neighbors.SpecificNPCs.LoveDryad: "{NPCName}? Oh, yeah, she's REALLY pretty! I definitely wanna paint her more...both outside and inside my gut......mmmmm...such a [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:deliciously] colorful dryad..."
	}

	Steampunker: {
		Content: I'm jolly good enough, thanks.

		Neighbors: {
			SpecificNPCs: {
				LoveCyborg: It's quite a good show, having {NPCName} around. The old bucket of bolts and I always have plenty of lovely things to chit and chat about!
				LikePainter: The painter? Yeah, {NPCName}'s a good sort. Spruces up my works all the time! Plenty nice bloke, he is, save for how often I end up tuning up his system. Can't say I blame him; he's always awfully hungry, and he's got good taste to be snackin' on me so much!
				HateMechanic: "{NPCName}? She can put a sock right in it, for all I care! I'm NOT falling for her gaudy gizmos and gadgets!"
			}
		}
	}

	Enigma: {
		Content: Nothin' too crazy going on.
		NoHome: I have two questions. 1. Where the fuck am I? 2. Do you... have some place I can stay at?
		FarFromHome: I think... I got lost. Whoops!

		Biomes: {
			Mushroom: It's... beautiful. Sure, the mushrooms are somewhat inedible, which is a shame...but blue is such a nice color! I love it here!!!
			Hallow: This place is pretty and everything tastes like candy! But those DAMN gastropods...I HATE THOSE!!! So, it kinda evens out, this place is nice.
			Jungle: There's something about this place that just... makes my magic power thingymajigs... easier to do? Not complaining at all!
			Desert: It is hot as hell in this fucky ass hot ass room im in! How is nobody else complaining about the heat???
			Tundra: One time I slipped on ice. I now hold a grudge against ice for the rest of my life.
			Corruption: This place, sucks. That's all there really is to say on the matter.
			Crimson: This place, sucks. That's all there really is to say on the matter.
			Underworld: Yeesh, I might just pass out from being in here. Unfortunately for me, the Underworld isn't a separate biome according to happiness metrics, so I'm forced to be neutral about this. Ugh.
			Dungeon: This place, sucks. That's all there really is to say on the matter.
		}

		Neighbors: {
			CrowdLevel: {
				Alone: Can't complain about isolation, I guess. I'm not that good at socializing...
				GoodCompany: There's a few nice people around, it's great!
				BadCompany: Few people around is...alright? Don't really appreciate the few that are here though...
				GoodCrowd: Wow, that's quite the amount of people!
				NeutralCrowd: Wow, that's quite the amount of people!..,eugh...
				BadCrowd: Why them. Of all people. Why?
			}

			SpecificNPCs: {
				LoveTruffle: "{NPCName} is such a silly guy, I love him!.. What, did you expect me to say fun guy? Nah."
				LikePrincess: Ah, the princess. She's fun to hang out with, but I'm kinda running out of stuff to change the topic to everytime she asks about my 'magical items', since they aren't quite...for her age.
				LikeAngler: Fish are so cool! And {NPCName} understands that! Most people seem to find him annoying though, but I think his attitude makes him funnier!
				HateTaxCollector: "{NPCName}..? Fuck that guy, I need my money to buy sweets!"
			}
		}
	}
}

Bestiary: {
	Meteorite: {
		MeteorMarble: A small, curious construct which is never (at first) seen without its numerous small rocks orbiting its core. The core's inside is something of a compressive cage that burns anything (and, if made possible, anyONE) that enters.
		MeteorMaiden: A fascinating woman-like construct, though built without the waist or anything under. The top and bottom halves of her torso can separate seemingly-infinitely to reveal a magically-formed stomach which torches anything inside.
	}

	Sky.Observer: Every so often, a Demon Eye sees much more than it is meant to see in its life as a result of a defect. This, of course, leads to the eye becoming far too large to move freely about the skies. While functionally harmless due to being calmed by the weights of knowledge, their sheer size makes them hard to swallow without good practice.
	Underworld.HellHarpy: Harpies are often kidnapped and carted to the Underworld via Desperai's innumerable ingredient hunters. Some of these harpies escape the gluttony of demonkind, though...but not without adjustments to their figure and form. A few demons might still be jostling around on any given one's chest and thighs.
	Mushroom.OversizedFairy: Okay, first of all, no idea how you'd unlock this entry. But good job.

	TownNPCs: {
		Succubus: Having lived on the outskirts of Desperai for many years before deciding to pack up and leave, Lucinda's a demon that just wants people to believe she's a strong, independent predator who doesn't NEED no stupid charms!...even though she can barely hold her prey the same way her superiors could.
		Enigma: A silly girl with silly creation magic. She made her equipment herself, but at the time, didn't know how to make a color other than green. Her favourite color is actually blue, but she thinks it'd be weird if she suddenly changed her whole color scheme.
		StPromethia: An intensely masochistic Amateur Saint to the Songstress of the Divine, St. Promethia'd love nothing more than to be a heaping helping of fat on any predator she finds...and, of course, her job as a walking, talking gastrointestinal medicine ends up letting her do this very often.
	}
}

NPCs: {
	LucindaBound.DisplayName: Succubus

	Lucinda: {
		DisplayName: Succubus

		TownNPCMood: {
			Content: Aside from you not fillin' out my gut right now, I think I'm fine.
			NoHome: My stomach's a good spot for a mortal morsel like you, but I need a real place to live if I'm gonna feed this gut of mine on the regular.
			FarFromHome: Well, I've headed off a little far from home today, eh? Then again, it's all worth gettin' the right meal.
			LoveSpace: I love having so much space.
			DislikeCrowded: I dislike how crowded I am.
			HateCrowded: I hate how crowded I am.
			LoveBiome: It's great to be around the ocean, don'tcha think? Sittin' in the warm sand, lookin' over the sunset as your prey-stuffed gut churns and gurgles even the meatiest meals into more of ya...it's the BEST. My only regret's that I didn't come up here sooner.
			LikeBiome: The desert's nice and warm, I have to say. Reminds me of home, in all the good ways, and it's a lot more open to boot. Plenty of good prey to snatch up, too, if you know where to look. I like it.
			DislikeBiome: It's way too cold around here, if you ask me. Food's a bit too fluffy for me, too. I'd kill for a warm lava bath right now; find me one, or at least a warmer place to crash.
			HateBiome: Seriously!? This place is awful! I can't even eat the stuff here; I might get food poisonin' from how rotten it all is!
			LoveNPC: I love {NPCName}.
			LikeNPC: I like {NPCName}.
			DislikeNPC: I dislike {NPCName}.
			HateNPC: I hate {NPCName}.
			LikeNPC_Princess: I like {NPCName}.
			Princess_LovesNPC: I like {NPCName}.
		}

		HelpButton: {
			DisplayName: Guidance

			Tips: {
				Intro:
					'''
					Lookin' to stay out of a pred's gut, huh? Well, I guess I can give ya a few tips.
					Just be warned, I'll be givin' you everything I've got if you end up in MY gut; I'm just makin' sure nobody else gets ya first.
					'''
				PredStats:
					'''
					There are four main parts to any pred's digestive system: [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:throat strength, stomach strength, acid strength, and absorption strength].
					Each one measures a different aspect of how well a gut and its friends can handle your food. Those terms are mainly used by the more...science-y types, though, so I'll keep it simple for ya.
					'''
				SwallowSize:
					'''
					A pred's throat can only handle so much before it starts to hurt. That's called their [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:swallow capacity] on paper.
					The higher it is, the bigger the meals that can fit down their gullet, and the easier smaller meals go down. Simple enough, yeah?
					So, don't wanna get eaten? Steer clear of preds that can get you down easy until you're sure you can gulp 'em down yourself.
					'''
				StomachCapacity:
					'''
					Just like your throat, [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:your gut can only hold so much] before it starts complainin'.
					People have put together a ton of tools for that in this day and age, though....not that I ever need 'em.
					If you can [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:bring some bulky stuff or a few friends] into a gut with you, I'm sure any pred'll feel the heartburn in no time.
					'''
				Struggles:
					'''
					Obviously, things don't like bein' in bellies most of the time; to get out, you'll have to [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:fight your way out] of there as long as you can.
					Just be sure you don't run outta air or the acids don't get to you too quick. [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:Can't really fight back if you're already knocked out...]
					'''
				Stomachache:
					'''
					If you fight around too much, you'll [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:give your pred a bellyache], which usually brings 'em right back up.
					Just be sure you don't end up food for a masochist if you have to kick around a lot to get out of their gut. 
					'''
				Absorption:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.BadThingVore}:Once a pred's acids get their meal knocked out, or they run outta air], their gut can start [c/{$Mods.V2.Colors.GoodThingVore}:properly processin' that meal] into a nice sludge.
					All you gotta do is keep yourself from gettin' to that point, and you're golden. That's just about all I can tell ya; it really is as simple as that.
					'''
				AlreadyDinnerForADemon:
					'''
					Help? What kinda help? Help gettin' mulched?

					...no, really. Don't you have some thick demon thighs to be fillin' out right about now?
					Seriously, if you got gulped this easy, you're a pretty lousy pred...
					'''
				Invalid: ...what was I talkin' about again?
			}
		}

		FreeButton.DisplayName: Free
		DontFreeBecauseYoureAnAssholeButton.DisplayName: Don't Free
		Census.SpawnCondition:
			'''
			Find and free her in the Underworld
			Whether you're nice about it or not doesn't matter
			'''
	}

